nd Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T21:51:48-07:00","id":1392416,"title":"","content":"Also I gotta say... LOVE IT! Fucking nerd that I am I went to the Teros first and I love everything about them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T01:07:05-07:00","id":1392440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392367#post1392367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. It's awesome - the explicit thematic is &amp;quot;science fantasy mythology&amp;quot;; one gets the sense that the divine and science aren't really different things in the Atlantean view of things, and it informs their myths; yes, <i>of course </i>Badarus wants a starship, he's the God of <i>Shipwrights</i>. It's his <i>job.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>FINALLY, I can run my Stargate inpired Atlantis &amp; Universe game on Scion! \u2764\ufe0f Starships made by Theros!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/0HyD3aKFTkA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/0HyD3aKFTkA\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/0HyD3aKFTkA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/0HyD3aKFTkA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T03:42:06-07:00","id":1392471,"title":"","content":"I'm going through my copy right now. So far, I'm loving what I'm seeing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T05:10:47-07:00","id":1392481,"title":"","content":"Quick question for anyone who\u2019s read this book<br /> <br /> What is the general time frame for Atlantis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T05:30:02-07:00","id":1392482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392481#post1392481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question for anyone who\u2019s read this book<br /> <br /> What is the general time frame for Atlantis?</div> </div> </div> </div>... And is there pointed location of Atlantis in Scion universe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T06:54:48-07:00","id":1392499,"title":"","content":"Also, it's actually written the Deva-Yazata rivalry really well; it's an Order-Chaos split. <br /> <br /> See, the Yazata idea of &quot;good&quot; is fundamentally wrapped up in &quot;free will&quot;; even when they dictate morality, it's couched in terms of Honesty; you aren't bossing people around, you're calling a spade a spade, an evil act an evil act. The idea of a true caste system or acceptance of karma as a thing is something they find inexplicable and a little horrifying.<br /> <br /> Of course, that also leads to their major flaws as a pantheon; they think that they not only understand morality better than anyone else, they're also rather gullible. They simply don't understand why anyone would want to lie, especially for altruistic reasons. So it's very possible to get them pointing the wrong direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T07:06:07-07:00","id":1392505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392481#post1392481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question for anyone who\u2019s read this book<br /> <br /> What is the general time frame for Atlantis?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little confused on this. What do you mean by time frame? The described Atlantean culture is written up to be modern day, but with their divine super science. As far as when they largely shut themselves off from the world, it's a vaguely nebulous &quot;in the past&quot;. For their tech... well they're kind of DC's New Gods, or Island Wakanda, so it's super tech, but not necessarily how we would have gotten there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T07:52:27-07:00","id":1392529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AutoDefenestrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392505#post1392505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little confused on this. What do you mean by time frame? The described Atlantean culture is written up to be modern day, but with their divine super science. As far as when they largely shut themselves off from the world, it's a vaguely nebulous &amp;quot;in the past&amp;quot;. For their tech... well they're kind of DC's New Gods, or Island Wakanda, so it's super tech, but not necessarily how we would have gotten there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, there's an implication Atlantis doesn't know what disaster caused the Teros to flee to Earth. Or what caused the city to sink to begin with.<br /> <br /> Kinda want to make a fan book of their myths, now...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T08:35:29-07:00","id":1392547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392529#post1392529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, there's an implication Atlantis doesn't know what disaster caused the Teros to flee to Earth. Or what caused the city to sink to begin with.<br /> <br /> Kinda want to make a fan book of their myths, now...</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn\u2019t any reference I saw to the city being sunken in the Atlantis still exists option. The only reference to it being sunken is discussing the canon default, where it is dead and gone as Plato described.<br /> <br /> Except for the celestial creator twins, the Teros are from Earth, but they and the humans of Atlantis are described as initially having arrived on the island as refugees, before the twins descended with their god-tech gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T09:39:22-07:00","id":1392578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392547#post1392547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There isn\u2019t any reference I saw to the city being sunken in the Atlantis still exists option. The only reference to it being sunken is discussing the canon default, where it is dead and gone as Plato described.<br /> <br /> Except for the celestial creator twins, the Teros are from Earth, but they and the humans of Atlantis are described as initially having arrived on the island as refugees, before the twins descended with their god-tech gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. I misread that.<br /> <br /> Still, Atlantis has suffered at least one catastrophe, namely pissing off the local nature goddess so much she threw a spear made of anti-math at it and proclaimed that urban sprawl was now punishable by death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T10:15:14-07:00","id":1392585,"title":"","content":"I mean the Atlantis section starts with &quot;The default assumption is that Atlantis in the World is dead. However, if you want Atlantis-&quot; and then it gives a brief primer.<br /> <br /> The time is &quot;Atlantis has existed for a long time, and still does to this day&quot;<br /> <br /> The location is &quot;Zipped up somewhere along the <i>Z</i> axis so that people from outside can't easily find it&quot;<br /> <br /> But I presume it's somewhere in the Atlantic Ocean, possibly somewhere in the Mediterranean Sea","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T10:31:06-07:00","id":1392589,"title":"","content":"Sigh. Considering how much I really really want to have this book I think I will need to walk away because its quite sad that I can't get it right now. Atlantis is my jam and to have another version to be able to yoink from is just just brilliant. <br /> <br /> Like I might not ever use it in Scion but I could see using it as a Flux based realm for say a Trinity Continuum Adventure! or Aberrant game. I mean, heck, replace Scion with Nova and its not really suuuuuper different, hehe. <br /> <br /> But yeah, I want this. And unless Onyx Path provides some way for me to pre-buy it like right now, which I would do, in a heartbeat, I will have to wait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T10:34:31-07:00","id":1392592,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys. That helps with the Atlantis issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T10:35:52-07:00","id":1392593,"title":"","content":"I keep feeling a little uncomfortable with the concept but I realize it\u2019s me overthinking things. Because it\u2019s a Wakanda homage, but Wakanda\u2019s narrative is making a point about the impact of colonialism on Africa. Without that it comes off to me as \u201cundiluted utopia through isolation\u201d, when of course in reality isolation creates stagnation while your non-isolationist neighbors keep advancing, just look at the Ming Dynasty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T10:40:01-07:00","id":1392595,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> agreed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T10:48:56-07:00","id":1392598,"title":"","content":"While I obviously don't have the book the whole image of the isolated civilization that is more advanced then the outside world is a motiff much older than wakanda, for all that said nation has been pushed to the popular mindset. I have books decades on one my shelf where they talk about the hidden utopia slash society slash whatever. <br /> <br /> A country that has the tech level of modern society tens of thousands of years BCE isn't going to suddenly stop being a powerful nation just because it isolates. Also isolates doesn't mean ignorance, though this last point is said without having the book. The country may isolate itself but still have operations elsewhere - be it on other worlds or throughout the Earth itself. They may know about Earths history without letting themselves be a part of it. <br /> <br /> As an aside when the other option for a super advanced nation is conquest then isolation is probably the best idea. When you look out and all you see is people living in crude wooden huts when you are sailing the stars on ships of light and creating constructions of tech and magic and living in cities you either leave them alone or you expand and basically wipe them out through assimilation or conquest or actual death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T11:28:58-07:00","id":1392608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392593#post1392593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep feeling a little uncomfortable with the concept but I realize it\u2019s me overthinking things. Because it\u2019s a Wakanda homage, but Wakanda\u2019s narrative is making a point about the impact of colonialism on Africa. Without that it comes off to me as \u201cundiluted utopia through isolation\u201d, when of course in reality isolation creates stagnation while your non-isolationist neighbors keep advancing, just look at the Ming Dynasty.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's actually the point. The very Virtues of the Teros are Nostalgia vs. Vision, and a big theme is that Atlantis is trapped in its own past and stagnated, with there being a growing rift among the Teros about whether they should remain isolated or emerge fully.<br /> <br /> Really, my problem is that we didn't see what the Titans' Purviews are (which is a shame, because they are also <i>so cool).</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T11:35:37-07:00","id":1392609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392608#post1392608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's actually the point. The very Virtues of the Teros are Nostalgia vs. Vision, and a big theme is that Atlantis is trapped in its own past and stagnated, with there being a growing rift among the Teros about whether they should remain isolated or emerge fully.<br /> <br /> Really, my problem is that we didn't see what the Titans' Purviews are (which is a shame, because they are also <i>so cool).</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably give Z_Z_Z some form of Deception.<br /> <br /> I also like to imagine that it's not pronounced &quot;Zzzzz&quot; but is actually best approximated by making that Internet Dial-Up noise. Specifically the crackly part <i>after</i> the &quot;BEEP BOOP BEEP BEEP BOOP&quot; part. Mostly because just imagine.<br /> <br /> Teros Hero: And then one of our greatest enemies- [Crackly static screech]<br /> <br /> Tuatha Hero: The fucking hell was THAT?!<br /> <br /> Teros: I mean she ate her own name and so best we can refer to her is that sound. Or calling her the Unspeaker.<br /> <br /> Tuatha: Do that from now on, <i>please</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T12:22:47-07:00","id":1392624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392608#post1392608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's actually the point. The very Virtues of the Teros are Nostalgia vs. Vision, and a big theme is that Atlantis is trapped in its own past and stagnated, with there being a growing rift among the Teros about whether they should remain isolated or emerge fully.<br /> <br /> Really, my problem is that we didn't see what the Titans' Purviews are (which is a shame, because they are also <i>so cool).</i></div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is nothing in the text tells me how they\u2019ve stagnated as they are still described as a technological utopia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T13:33:20-07:00","id":1392657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392499#post1392499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it's actually written the Deva-Yazata rivalry really well; it's an Order-Chaos split. <br /> <br /> See, the Yazata idea of &amp;quot;good&amp;quot; is fundamentally wrapped up in &amp;quot;free will&amp;quot;; even when they dictate morality, it's couched in terms of Honesty; you aren't bossing people around, you're calling a spade a spade, an evil act an evil act. The idea of a true caste system or acceptance of karma as a thing is something they find inexplicable and a little horrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Deva and Yazata have a lot of nuanced potential for conflict, chiefly in the nature of purity, the necessity of death, and the existence of good and evil... Where the Yazata believe Purity is precious and must be protected (hence why they keep dead bodies away from sacred fire) the Deva believe that Purity, especially of the divine, cannot be corrupted but instead purifies (hence why they throw dead bodies into sacred fire)... In addition, as the Pantheon of Paladins, the Yazata are deeply invested in the battle between Good and Evil, which for them is a fundamental part of their Cosmology... Meanwhile the Deva do not really have a concept of Good and Evil, only of Understanding and Ignorance... For them there is no opposing fundamental force in the universe promulgating evil, and even the Asura gain their powers from the greater Gods like the Trimurti... Finally, the Yazata see Death as an aberration of the plan of Creation, and their ultimate victory involves an end to it, but for the Deva Death is fundamental... All things will die, whether it takes them 30 mins or 300 trillion years.<br /> <br /> But the Deva themselves have never cared about the caste system... That's mostly just their priests and temples, the gods time and again ignore it. But it is fitting that it is a point on which the conflict occurs because a lot of conflict between the two likely does stem from such misunderstandings... Ganesha after all is both Deva and Yazata, just like Vayu, and anyone who gets these two to co-operate has likely just created one of the most terrifying Divine Alliances of all time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T14:50:54-07:00","id":1392681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392624#post1392624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is nothing in the text tells me how they\u2019ve stagnated as they are still described as a technological utopia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. They explicitly have been under the same immortal aristocracy for centuries and have accepted the dogma of things as truth. Also a big theme, and explicitly made in the in-universe development process, is that of &quot;potential hubris-induced catastrophe.&quot; I think that a lot of the nuance was cut in favor of the make-a-pantheon system, and understandably so, but I don't think you're supposed to view it as a utopia, just a place that has found a happy status quo for centuries - a genuinely functional one, making it a place worth saving, but a place with social problems that are one disaster away from becoming major ones. One of their Titans is explicitly the embodiment of heterodoxy and selfish misappropriation of existing ideals for a reason - it also strikes me as a place that could easily spit out a megalomaniac who thinks it's just for Atlantis to conquer the world, and for them to conquer Atlantis as the most perfect product of their genetic engineering (and one look at the super-soldiers and &quot;genetically implanted tactical consciousnesses&quot; pretty much hit every little bit of bodily autonomy horror I have).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T17:06:39-07:00","id":1392700,"title":"","content":"Soooo, from reading things here and notes elsewhere this is mostly the Pantheon stuff right, so will be getting material on Atlantis as a location? Maybe in a book about creating mythic places and such. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T17:27:51-07:00","id":1392702,"title":"","content":"I don't recall anything about Atlantis as a location. It's entirely about the people, and mainly about the Pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T17:43:07-07:00","id":1392707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392702#post1392702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall anything about Atlantis as a location. It's entirely about the people, and mainly about the Pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Atlantis is Mars. I thought everybody knew that.;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T19:17:10-07:00","id":1392721,"title":"","content":"Enough about Atlantis - talk me about real selling point of the book ( Atlantis is only cherry on that for me ) - <b>the Myth Levels!</b> We got some spoilers about year and half ago. Did we got real mechanics on those, beside those descriptions? Some proper rules or hacks for running, like, Iron Myth Levels games? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Full <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/mysteries-of-the-world-scion-2e/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Myth Levels Blog post</b></a> - Here is spoilers sum-up:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myth Levels preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>CHAPTER ONE: MYTH LEVEL</b><br /> <br /> The Myth Level is five options along four axes of design, meant to allow the Storyguide to choose how many of Scion\u2019s setting \u201cdials\u201d they want to crank. This chapter lays out what each of those dials looks like at each of the five Myth Levels. Those Myth Levels are:<ul><li><b>Iron:</b> Perfectly mundane. Very similar in nature and tone to Gaiman\u2019s <b><i>American Gods</i></b>, where ifriti are cab drivers, Odhinn is a shiftless wandering con man, and Chernobog and the goddesses of dawn, midday and evening are poor immigrants scraping by in a shitty apartment in Chicago.</li> <li><b>Heroic: </b>Mostly mundane, but with room for great acts of heroism. Most supernatural creatures still have mundane manifestations here (that centaur is still just a biker here), but Scions and gods may appear as impressive and tremendous \u2013 Aphrodite isn\u2019t some burnt out barfly here, she\u2019s drop-dead gorgeous and probably on fashion covers. This is the level of the <b><i>Iliad</i> </b>and the <i><b>Odyssey</b></i>.</li> <li><b>Bronze: </b>This is where the supernatural really comes into play. Creatures of Legend shed their mundane disguises in areas of Bronze Myth, and appear in their true nature. Magic becomes overt here, and Demigods wield their true power. This is <b><i>Clash of the Titans</i></b> territory, and there might just actually be dragons in that undetailed area of the map.</li> <li><b>Silver: </b>Past the threshold of urban myth and getting into epic fantasy, places of Silver Myth are deeply resonant with Myth. They are often fanciful places and hidden vales of magic technically found in the World, but not of it. The power of a creature of Legend is reflected in its appearance \u2013 the mightier the entity, the more impressive it appears. Zelazny\u2019s <i><b>Lord of Light</b> </i>goes into this area of Myth in its narrative.</li> <li><b>Gold:</b> Flat-out mythological, where symbolism is the same as its reality. Places of Gold Myth are not even of this World. Lots of <b>Scion</b> 1e went into this territory, with its otherworldly locales, and lots of fantasy that touches on extradimensional areas and the like qualify.</li> </ul>The trick is this: you should be able to choose a starting Myth Level and then turn each dial up or down within that level to taste. So, for instance, as Storyguide I might choose to start at the Iron Level but crank the Titanomachy up, turning <b><i>American Gods</i></b> into a raging shadow war that you have to keep peeling back layers of the World to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T19:42:39-07:00","id":1392729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392721#post1392721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enough about Atlantis - talk me about real selling point of the book ( Atlantis is only cherry on that for me ) - <b>the Myth Levels!</b> We got some spoilers about year and half ago. Did we got real mechanics on those, beside those descriptions? Some proper rules or hacks for running, like, Iron Myth Levels games? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Full <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/mysteries-of-the-world-scion-2e/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Myth Levels Blog post</b></a> - Here is spoilers sum-up:</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, The whole first chapter is based on this. Each Myth Level is given a paragraph general description, then it goes through the 5 categories of Genre, Theocentrism, Titanomachy, and Evidence, each category giving how it effects the World of the 5 Myth Levels, giving a decent idea of how to run a game at each level. There are also a side-bar focusing on each specific Myth Level, combining the info of each category together to give a quick idea of how a game at that level might play and a good inspiration or 2 to look at for that Myth Level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/898-kurasu","name":"kurasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T19:58:02-07:00","id":1392731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392721#post1392721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enough about Atlantis - talk me about real selling point of the book ( Atlantis is only cherry on that for me ) - <b>the Myth Levels!</b> We got some spoilers about year and half ago. Did we got real mechanics on those, beside those descriptions? Some proper rules or hacks for running, like, Iron Myth Levels games? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Full <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/mysteries-of-the-world-scion-2e/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Myth Levels Blog post</b></a> - Here is spoilers sum-up:</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what the bulk of Chapter One is all about. There are four main dials that you can twist: genre, theocentrism, Titanomachy, and evidence. Iron genre is gritty street-level stuff; gold genre is wildly over the top. Iron theocentrism has at most one Pantheon in play, and may even have none; gold theocentrism is the default arrangement where all mythologies are 100% true. Iron Titanomachy has the Titans bring largely irrelevant; gold Titanomachy involves open warfare with the Titans. Iron evidence is the World of Darkness style of \u201call supernatural activity remains in the shadows\u201d, while gold evidence is the opposite: a Mythical World where nothing is concealed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T02:26:35-07:00","id":1392775,"title":"","content":"There are rules options for each Myth Level under each 'dial', though not every dial has an mechanical effect. Evidence has more of a mechanical impact than say, Titanmachy, which would be represented narratively.<br /> <br /> I am more concerned about my ability to understand the Cult birthright. The sample ones appear to be stronger than their rating suggests, unless I am misunderstanding something. And I can't report it as errata, because I could just be an idiot who can't see how it is meant to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T04:25:04-07:00","id":1392781,"title":"","content":"You can really do interesting things by putting the myth dials at differents settings. They dont all need to be at gold or iron.<br /> For example the standard settkng for the World is.<br /> Genre : Bronze<br /> Theocentrism : Gold<br /> Titanomachy : Silver<br /> Evidence : Silver","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T23:09:38-07:00","id":1393013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392775#post1392775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am more concerned about my ability to understand the Cult birthright. The sample ones appear to be stronger than their rating suggests, unless I am misunderstanding something. And I can't report it as errata, because I could just be an idiot who can't see how it is meant to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you asking about Light and Shadow?<br /> <br /> Basically, when you start, the foundation step has you with 2 points to allocate however you want. And then for each Cult Rating dot, you get another point to allocate. Which means Cult Rating = Light + Shadow - 1. This rule is stated across page 23/24. Does that help? (It threw me for a loop on first reading, too, so I had to go back and look for the citation.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T00:00:56-07:00","id":1393020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392781#post1392781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can really do interesting things by putting the myth dials at differents settings. They dont all need to be at gold or iron.<br /> For example the standard settkng for the World is.<br /> Genre : Bronze<br /> Theocentrism : Gold<br /> Titanomachy : Silver<br /> Evidence : Silver</div> </div> </div> </div>Default at Hero level at least. Genre is likely ascends as power level does.<br /> <br /> Origin tends toward Iron to Heroic, while Hero bridges Heroic to Bronze. Demigod is likely to land more into Silver, while Gods play in the Gold in the cosmic, but curve back around to Iron via Incarnations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T00:12:40-07:00","id":1393023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392781#post1392781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example the standard settkng for the World is.<br /> Genre : Bronze<br /> Theocentrism : Gold<br /> Titanomachy : Silver<br /> Evidence : Silver</div> </div> </div> </div>I trying to understand the Myth Levels 'rules' by this - so mark me where I'm wrong...<br /> <br /> Theocrentrism Gold ( Max ) mean the tag line 'All Myths are True'.<br /> Titanomachy Silver ( Near-Max ) mean 'Titan War can return any second, we fight more and more loose Titan forces'/.<br /> Evidance Silver ( Near-Max ) mean 'Gods presence is almost felt by everyone. SOME secrets are only left out', yes?<br /> <br /> I still trying to guess what Genre Bronze (Medium) mean here... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> EDIT: Posted when <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> wrote they post. Okay, so Genre is general powerlevel of story itself...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-31-2020, 03:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T00:36:53-07:00","id":1393028,"title":"","content":"So my hombrewed <b>Scion</b> chronicle would look like in Myth Levels how? Let's write a sum-up of basis of it to various parts of Myths:<br /> <br /> <i>'Story about simple people slowly introduced to world of Gods and Heroes - as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275725-2e-setting-hack-gods-in-hiding-and-new-mythic-age\"><b>Gods Are In Hiding</b></a>. At least major religion and Myths are true, even when Earth has more or less stable history to this point. Titans where secret threat for centuries - now, with Global Warming, new Titan War will restart. However, all of that is outside of normal people do not - cannot - see it all. Oh, and Atlantis is returning on Earth...'</i><br /> <br /> So this chronicle would like:<br /> Genre Iron ( Near Min ) -&gt; Bronze - Generally casual plots with 'some myths were beside it' and uncovering world of Gods - until players go to Hero Tier and start to be Involved in new Titan War<br /> Theocrentrism Bronze ( Middle ) - All major Pantheons of corebooks exists. Rest is not sure / only on story needs.<br /> Titanomachy Iron ( Min ) -&gt; Silver - It would mean that starting status quo is 'Secret Cold War with Titans' that in time of Hero Tier goes to almost open conflict with them.<br /> Evidance Iron ( Min ) - Gods and Pantheons are secret to population at large, separated from them by Mythic Mists.<br /> <br /> I judge it right?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T00:53:50-07:00","id":1393030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392499#post1392499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it's actually written the Deva-Yazata rivalry really well; it's an Order-Chaos split.<br /> <br /> See, the Yazata idea of &quot;good&quot; is fundamentally wrapped up in &quot;free will&quot;; even when they dictate morality, it's couched in terms of Honesty; you aren't bossing people around, you're calling a spade a spade, an evil act an evil act. The idea of a true caste system or acceptance of karma as a thing is something they find inexplicable and a little horrifying.<br /> <br /> Of course, that also leads to their major flaws as a pantheon; they think that they not only understand morality better than anyone else, they're also rather gullible. They simply don't understand why anyone would want to lie, especially for altruistic reasons. So it's very possible to get them pointing the wrong direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>This only makes me want to play them MORE.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392731#post1392731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That's what the bulk of Chapter One is all about. There are four main dials that you can twist: genre, theocentrism, Titanomachy, and evidence. Iron genre is gritty street-level stuff; gold genre is wildly over the top. Iron theocentrism has at most one Pantheon in play, and may even have none; gold theocentrism is the default arrangement where all mythologies are 100% true. Iron Titanomachy has the Titans bring largely irrelevant; gold Titanomachy involves open warfare with the Titans. Iron evidence is the World of Darkness style of \u201call supernatural activity remains in the shadows\u201d, while gold evidence is the opposite: a Mythical World where nothing is concealed.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I WANT TO PLAY WITH THE DIALS! </span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I throw money at the screen but the book does not appear! Why?! </span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T01:15:59-07:00","id":1393035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392624#post1392624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is nothing in the text tells me how they\u2019ve stagnated as they are still described as a technological utopia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, by its very definition, a utopia is stagnate. Once you have become perfect, there is no need to change, because if there was a need, then you weren't perfect. And if you did change, then you stop being perfect. That's only with a platonic ideal of perfection though. In the sense of a place where any sort of human need, hardship, or danger has been eliminated, be it with magic, technology, or whatever, you always run the risk of societel complacency or arrogance, both of which can lead to stagation.<br /> I've not read any of it, but with their Virtues, it sounds like one of their themes and a good potential focus for Atlantean centered stories is the temptation to admire what is or what was vs the drive to imagine what might be. It makes me really want to do an Atlantean centered game based on Silver Age superhero comics set around 1960.<br /> <br /> BRING ME THE DIALS!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T04:21:55-07:00","id":1393054,"title":"","content":"Double-post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-31-2020, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T04:27:48-07:00","id":1393055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392499#post1392499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it's actually written the Deva-Yazata rivalry really well; it's an Order-Chaos split. <br /> <br /> See, the Yazata idea of &quot;good&quot; is fundamentally wrapped up in &quot;free will&quot;; even when they dictate morality, it's couched in terms of Honesty; you aren't bossing people around, you're calling a spade a spade, an evil act an evil act. The idea of a true caste system or acceptance of karma as a thing is something they find inexplicable and a little horrifying.<br /> <br /> Of course, that also leads to their major flaws as a pantheon; they think that they not only understand morality better than anyone else, they're also rather gullible. They simply don't understand why anyone would want to lie, especially for altruistic reasons. So it's very possible to get them pointing the wrong direction.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1392657#post1392657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Deva and Yazata have a lot of nuanced potential for conflict, chiefly in the nature of purity, the necessity of death, and the existence of good and evil... Where the Yazata believe Purity is precious and must be protected (hence why they keep dead bodies away from sacred fire) the Deva believe that Purity, especially of the divine, cannot be corrupted but instead purifies (hence why they throw dead bodies into sacred fire)... In addition, as the Pantheon of Paladins, the Yazata are deeply invested in the battle between Good and Evil, which for them is a fundamental part of their Cosmology... Meanwhile the Deva do not really have a concept of Good and Evil, only of Understanding and Ignorance... For them there is no opposing fundamental force in the universe promulgating evil, and even the Asura gain their powers from the greater Gods like the Trimurti... Finally, the Yazata see Death as an aberration of the plan of Creation, and their ultimate victory involves an end to it, but for the Deva Death is fundamental... All things will die, whether it takes them 30 mins or 300 trillion years.<br /> <br /> But the Deva themselves have never cared about the caste system... That's mostly just their priests and temples, the gods time and again ignore it. But it is fitting that it is a point on which the conflict occurs because a lot of conflict between the two likely does stem from such misunderstandings... Ganesha after all is both Deva and Yazata, just like Vayu, and anyone who gets these two to co-operate has likely just created one of the most terrifying Divine Alliances of all time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just to add to this for others who haven\u2019t benefited from Discord conversations on the topic: I\u2019d also suggest the Yazata belief in OBJECTIVE TRUTH chafes against the understanding of Maya and (building on Samudra\u2019s point about there not being cosmic Good and Evil) the unity of perceived as separate things.<br /> <br /> It goes to why the Deception purview frequently shows up for benevolent reality weavers among the Deva, while the concept is so anathemic to the Yazata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-31-2020, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T03:16:07-07:00","id":1393384,"title":"","content":"The book's crafting section has an example where the scion crafts a relic, should we be assuming that they're a demigod in the example or is there a new rule somewhere which lets heroes attempt tier 3 crafting projects that I missed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 06-01-2020, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T08:08:27-07:00","id":1393639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1393384#post1393384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book's crafting section has an example where the scion crafts a relic, should we be assuming that they're a demigod in the example or is there a new rule somewhere which lets heroes attempt tier 3 crafting projects that I missed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Devs confirmed it\u2019s an oversight that needs clarification and it\u2019s been submitted by multiple people for errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-03-2020, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T01:04:34-07:00","id":1393751,"title":"","content":"Just a quick question: When will it be available for the general public, e.g. people that could not back it due to not owning a credit card?<br /> Cause my group and I are really looking forward to it as to be able to upgrade our chars from 1e to 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11025-ganruy","name":"Ganruy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T06:47:02-07:00","id":1393772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ganruy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1393751#post1393751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a quick question: When will it be available for the general public, e.g. people that could not back it due to not owning a credit card?<br /> Cause my group and I are really looking forward to it as to be able to upgrade our chars from 1e to 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Your bank debit card can do the same jobs as a credit card.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T08:28:09-07:00","id":1393780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ganruy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1393751#post1393751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a quick question: When will it be available for the general public, e.g. people that could not back it due to not owning a credit card?<br /> Cause my group and I are really looking forward to it as to be able to upgrade our chars from 1e to 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately it could be weeks, or longer","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T08:35:02-07:00","id":1393782,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a> I have a credit card, but I didn\u2019t back the Kickstarter. Can I get it on BackerKit now or do I have to wait for the general public?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T08:49:28-07:00","id":1393785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1393782#post1393782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I have a credit card, but I didn\u2019t back the Kickstarter. Can I get it on BackerKit now or do I have to wait for the general public?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you could, I'd be doing that. I think you have to wait for pre-ordering. But maybe some kind wise soul will enlighten us with better options.<br /> <br /> If so, thank you ahead of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T13:08:57-07:00","id":1393831,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a> thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T13:55:17-07:00","id":1393850,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, I'm unaware of any way to get to the Companion now outside of using a time machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T13:58:17-07:00","id":1393852,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, the only books you could buy from the Backers Kit if you didn\u2019t back it and wanted it before release are Origin and Hero, that are for sale now. The other books were never available until... well... being available to everyone.<br /> <br /> I had this issue with Mythic Denizens, as I didn\u2019t back for physical copies, and had to wait for a few weeks before it was released. As Companion is a bit larger than Mythic Denizens, I think it will take a bit longer, but it\u2019s not going to be too long for sure, I would say a month or so.<br /> <br /> Sory to bring bad news...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T22:43:34-07:00","id":1393957,"title":"","content":"Well thanks to Corvid-19 and the restrictions we have in Germany a month is not that much of bad news.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11025-ganruy","name":"Ganruy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T05:12:19-07:00","id":1394021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ganruy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1393957#post1393957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well thanks to Corvid-19 and the restrictions we have in Germany a month is not that much of bad news.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least your infection rate has a solid downward curve. Due to the Red(reactionary) Blue(anything else) political divide, the red states are heading for a major wave of infections. <br /> <br /> So don't be glum. Life could be worse and a scrap or two of cheeriness gives you strength to share with others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T22:18:08-07:00","id":1394240,"title":"","content":"I have a doubt about the expanded Relic design. In the Relic Power: &quot;Grants one Boon appropriate to its motif, from a Purview it doesn\u2019t grant&quot;. It does mean that to get this 1 dot power the Relic MUST need to have a Purview attached?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23839-oxcelot","name":"Oxcelot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T22:24:22-07:00","id":1394242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oxcelot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1394240#post1394240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does mean that to get this 1 dot power the Relic MUST need to have a Purview attached?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it means 1 dot will give you one single effect of the purview, not access to marvels related to the purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T10:38:08-07:00","id":1394391,"title":"","content":"I admit I object to adding Boons to Relics on principle. In Hero we have a hard limit on Boons you can know, making the ones you pick be very important and say something about your character, with the gaps filled in by Marvels.<br /> <br /> And if you only need one Relic Dot for a Boon, well one, piss to that idea I guess who needs Marvels when you can just kit yourself out with Boons?<br /> <br /> And also <i>why are Boons cheaper than Knacks</i>, XP-wise? This makes the opposite of sense. Getting yourself a new Knack is 10XP, while getting a Boon via a Relic Dot is 5XP.<br /> <br /> Also several of the other Relic Abilities feel mispriced.<br /> <br /> Aggravated takes 4 Relic Dots? Does this mean that Aggravated if used as part of the base weapon's tags should cost 4 points? I mean I can see it if the Tag got buffed like I heard but I'd like that spelled out. Same for why Shockwave, a 4-point weapon tag, only 3 Relic Dots?<br /> <br /> Why is being able to summon and dismiss it a 2-dot power? That feels more like a 1-dot power. Especially if it takes an action to do so.<br /> <br /> 3 dots to give it a basic personality? That's just robbery, given that RAW you can instead invest 3 dots into making it a Guide that can give you access to a stunt AND maybe another Purview or an alternate Calling.<br /> <br /> (And yes I've submitted all this to Errata Feedback)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T10:55:50-07:00","id":1394395,"title":"","content":"When I read it, the way I see it, using the Relic boon (if you don\u2019t buy it thrice the regular ways) would require a marvel, but limited exclusively to that boon. It means, you need to pay extra legend.<br /> <br /> Its more like a very limited Purview, and not an extra known power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 06-05-2020, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T11:35:32-07:00","id":1394401,"title":"","content":"I mean if that's the case, it's not very clearly worded. I took it to mean &quot;Hey have a Boon, one dot&quot;<br /> <br /> I suppose another read of it could be &quot;Learn Boon from Purview X as a Boon from Purview Y&quot; which... Well that's kind of a silly thing to charge for, since I'd let my players just do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T12:58:21-07:00","id":1394412,"title":"","content":"It agains, like the other books, Mysteries of the World has some parts poorly written and it is sad. I'm not trying to rant, but as a constructive critique. Scion is really bad written in comparison to some recent RPGs I've read. Few things are really clear. I'm playing in a campaign with Mateus Luz and we had the same question because the way it is worded it can be interpreted in many different ways. The only exemples I've seen that use this idea of a boon in a Relic were the Relics in Book 2 where it has a Purview and grant access to a one dot boon from another Purview, BUT it still is not clear if the player CAN use one of their slots to pick that boon, or gains it free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23839-oxcelot","name":"Oxcelot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T13:26:11-07:00","id":1394419,"title":"","content":"Well that's what the errata feedback links are for. I quite love Scion and that's why I'm making earmarks in the parts I think the Companion should be adjusted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T13:54:10-07:00","id":1394427,"title":"","content":"I think the problem with Scion is it throws most of the limits of the powers to the &quot;common sense&quot; of the Story Guide and the players. The Devs used a certain mindset that they didn't delivered in the book.<br /> <br /> What I mean is let's say I have a Scion with a certain purview, for example War, War cover Strife in conceptual level as well as armed conflict. Can I use War to change someones biological sex? Its an conflict, a war between what the person feel and what its body forced to the person, so I could do that, same for Chaos changing the &quot;natural order&quot;, or Fertility making reproduction possible, or... well... any purview if you have enough imagination (the idea of changing someones sex came from an old discussion in this forum, so, sorry if it offends you).<br /> <br /> If you have players used to the more rigid system, like Mage (any of the 2), while they can bring a lot of ideas, they will probably stay inside the circles intended by the devs, if you have a group of players used to a more flexible system (like powered by Apocalypse, and other more modern systems) you can extend the powers beyond the usual.<br /> <br /> I guess, Kyman201 is one of the guys that have a more open way to see the limits, the same (in this case I am sure of it) for Oxcelot, while I am adept of a more rigid system (more in pair with Trinity Continuum).<br /> <br /> There are problems with Scion, as there are with any other game, but the main one in my view is how flexible it can be while we play a character that should be less flexible (we play Heroes, not gods, yet).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T13:57:42-07:00","id":1394428,"title":"","content":"For your examples, my litmus test is &quot;Can a player justify it to me?&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, they don't even have to have an in-depth justification. If they can provide one that makes sense to me after a few seconds, I'd probably allow it.<br /> <br /> So yes, I would allow someone to use Epic Strength to use a Remove Condition Marvel in order to punch the cold out of somebody. Does it make sense on any biological or physical level? Fuck no. Is it awesome? Yes. Did the player make some kind of link to justify it? Well that depends on if you, the GM, decide that &quot;I'm so strong I can punch the sick out of someone&quot; is good enough justification. I personally would go &quot;Fuck yeah it is, pay the Legend&quot;<br /> <br /> I do remember the topic of changing sex via a Marvel coming up, and I also seem to recall making a big post that boiled down to &quot;And here's a short list of Purviews I would allow a Hero to use to change the sex of a willing subject&quot; and it was a pretty long list. :P<br /> <br /> I don't think Scion is a game tone that really benefits from discouraging creativity and getting metaphorical or esoteric with its literal divine powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 06-05-2020, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T14:05:07-07:00","id":1394429,"title":"","content":"Honestly scion's greatest weakness is that its the first in its new system/mechanics.<br /> <br /> And with all games that have this problem i have found that each further book is just that little bit better in regards to its relationship with its mechanic.<br /> <br /> All in all, i will say that despite this i've found that scions pull through. <br /> <br /> For me the companion book. Especially the mythic dial section is an absolute blast to read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T15:31:26-07:00","id":1394440,"title":"","content":"The dials helps a lot how to &quot;explain your World&quot; to others. I would add a dial for power flexibility, Iron would be limited to a very strict set of effects (only obvious connections) while in Gold you can do whatever you want as long there is descent explanation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T16:50:39-07:00","id":1394454,"title":"","content":"It may be a bit tougher to do a Versatility Set of Dials, because yeah, Iron is &quot;Very Rigid, No Adjustments, You Can't Use Metaphorical Fire With Your Fire Purview Even Though A Sample Boon Lets You&quot;, and with Gold being the basic gameline assumption... Like, the heck would be Heroic on that dial?<br /> <br /> &quot;Be a little bit metaphorical&quot;? &quot;DM flips a coin to see if they allow this&quot;?<br /> <br /> And if your setting assumes that you're only using these Purviews in their most literal definition (setting aside that it's gonna have to be something you and the players agree on) then you'll probably have to go through and shave like, a third to half of the Purviews off of each God in the Corebook, because a lot of them use their Purviews in more metaphorical ways. Brigid, for instance, has Fire but rarely has anything to do with spraying fire from her hands, and very much focuses more on the Homey Hearth, the Flame of the Forge, and the Fires of Inspiration. So are those all invalid under your assumption?<br /> <br /> Like, it takes precisely zero mechanical adjustment to have a more literal-minded group of players go &quot;Yeah I'll use Water to break a water main and flood the street&quot; all the time, but what's actually GAINED by a player who REALLY wants to do something like &quot;Oh can I use Health to hit someone's pressure points and make them explode, Fist of the North Star Style?&quot; and the GM going &quot;I'unno, that seems a little out there&quot;? Like, does going &quot;No&quot; in this situation make the game better? Does encouraging your players to have some fun with the Purviews make things better for everyone? (Note: I'd hesitate to allow a One Hit Kill with any marvel unless it's a Trivial target but I'd allow Health to make Attack Marvels and the like by striking pressure points)<br /> <br /> Maybe it's different playstyle but I don't see how just flat-out denying attempts at being creative when players want to be makes it more enjoyable. If your table is more comfortable with more literal Purview focus, then by all means, stick there, but even in this case does it hurt the game when someone goes &quot;Well the moon controls the tide, so I'll use a Moon Marvel to imitate the Shifting Tides Boon&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T17:06:37-07:00","id":1394455,"title":"","content":"I am aware Scion 2e is flexible, but given that Miracles are limited both broadly (via Purview access) and tightly (via Motifs) I can't say agree with the idea that it is 'too easy' to create any number of effects. Even putting that aside, there is not a lot of Legend to spend, so there are hard limits. Seriously, a God can use 12 Miracles at most without any special abilities as far as I can tell.<br /> (Sacrifices and worshippers may allow for regaining Legend quickly at those levels...if the follow Hero tier rules, but seperate issue.)<br /> <br /> Am I missing something in that regard? Just flat out overlooking a detail that makes it a lot easier than I am envisioning?<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, the Boon Relic power question is something I am interested in. Extra Boons could, in theory, be overpowered. And just substituting one Purview for another in regards to Boons is something the Hero book does already (sidebar in the Beauty purview), so use a Relic dot on that?<br /> <br /> But the idea that Heroes can throw around Boons they don't have willy-billy is something I can't quite grasp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":".  Stupid Typos 06-05-2020, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T17:11:01-07:00","id":1394457,"title":"","content":"Hm the thing with the versatility dial is that it is already taken into account.<br /> The book does mention to not treat the dials as rigid things and that if you feel the need for the game to move a dial up or down then you should do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T17:37:13-07:00","id":1394460,"title":"","content":"I will use the example of my Sword. My character is a Scion of Odin and has a huge sword with the motif \u201cThe Sword that cuts thru anything\u201d. I added the Star boon Starry Path (that allow long range teleport out of combat), where the character Focus on the destine and cut a hole i reality and allow him to go to the destination. Using this power would require 2 Legend, as the original Boon costs 1 Legend. As my character is L1 he needs to make a sacrifice to activate the power, for now at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T17:59:22-07:00","id":1394464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1394460#post1394460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will use the example of my Sword. My character is a Scion of Odin and has a huge sword with the motif \u201cThe Sword that cuts thru anything\u201d. I added the Star boon Starry Path (that allow long range teleport out of combat), where the character Focus on the destine and cut a hole i reality and allow him to go to the destination. Using this power would require 2 Legend, as the original Boon costs 1 Legend. As my character is L1 he needs to make a sacrifice to activate the power, for now at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but if you have a GM who's not being unreasonable, couldn't you just use the Purview that's probably on the sword (otherwise how could it have gotten a Motif?) and use the Sword to make a Marvel, rather than wasting a Dot on just the one Boon? Since you're paying Marvel prices anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T19:19:55-07:00","id":1394479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1394464#post1394464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but if you have a GM who's not being unreasonable, couldn't you just use the Purview that's probably on the sword (otherwise how could it have gotten a Motif?) and use the Sword to make a Marvel, rather than wasting a Dot on just the one Boon? Since you're paying Marvel prices anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually if I read the Relic dot power, it has to be a Purview the Relic DOESN'T have. I didn't know that you would have to pay Marvel prices for the Relic Boon. I'd have ruled that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a>'s sword would use the normal cost for the Boon.<br /> Will double check the book, but what page does it say that on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T19:30:54-07:00","id":1394480,"title":"","content":"As was said before, Boons are extremely worthy, as you have a pretty small number of them even on higher Legend, so it is better to work like that than giving a free purview for possibly every dot in birthright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T19:45:09-07:00","id":1394483,"title":"","content":"See this is why I'd flat-out ban putting Boons on Relics. It just feels like it's trying to game the system. You want to do Marvels through a Relic? Put Purviews on it and make a Marvel with it. And if it's just &quot;Get a Boon from a different Purview&quot; for one dot then especially banned, because there's no way I'm letting Boons cost less than a flipping Knack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T13:06:42-07:00","id":1394611,"title":"","content":"The thing is, to me the problem I have with Scion is not the rules per se, but how it is written. Look at other RPGs that are even more flexible than Scion: Cortex Prime (or the older and awesome, Firefly, Smallville, Levrage, Marvel Heroic), The Spire, The Heart, Blades in the Dark, City of Mist, Dresden Files Accelerated, Ironsworn, Mutant City Blues, and others. They are all RPGs more narrative driven instead of mechanics driven, some have more detailed mechanics and systems, others have so few, but everyone of them are clearly written. The rule is X or Y, and is intended to do A or B, if the Game Moderator and the Table wants to change, now they know how to game behaves.<br /> <br /> Scion has the problem of a more narrative driven game baked inside a more mechanical driven game. Scion is like trying to make Fate or Powered by the Apocalypse inside the Chronicles of Darkness system. It can work, but either you make everything very clear or it will not achieve anything you intended.<br /> <br /> And yet, in the campaign that I'm the Storyguide here in Brazil, we are now after 14 sessions of a Origin campaign, transitioning the characters for Hero level, and the book still doesn't have all the errata in it (the digital version). We still have many doubts about what the system is really trying to say, still in the Hero book there are parts that contradicts each other, like the Knack section about the knacks everyone starts. Still there are references to parts in the book that either doesn't exist, or are not clearly defined, still there are tags that does the same thing other tags do (like Bashing and Stun).<br /> <br /> The other RPGs I mentioned are much more cheaper and present all the system much more clearly. If I want to play Scion as a Hero, I need to buy 2 books that still deliver a system where it can be difficulty to really understand what the devs intended. It is a critique about what the people on Scion have been doing. It is not to thrown people under the bus, but they need to take a closer look to these things and learn from their mistakes. Scion 2e is still a game I won't recommend to people if I must choose between recommending Scion or City of Mist, for example.<br /> <br /> When I Moderate games I try to always be the fairest possible, and as with the rules as written today, sometimes it is really hard, specially when dealing with Birthrights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23839-oxcelot","name":"Oxcelot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T13:17:43-07:00","id":1394614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1394483#post1394483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See this is why I'd flat-out ban putting Boons on Relics. It just feels like it's trying to game the system. You want to do Marvels through a Relic? Put Purviews on it and make a Marvel with it. And if it's just &quot;Get a Boon from a different Purview&quot; for one dot then especially banned, because there's no way I'm letting Boons cost less than a flipping Knack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for double-posting. This is one of the things I'm on the fence too. It is not clear in the book if it must have a purview first, thus making the relic at least 3 dots minimum, or if it can have only this power, or even if the boon is in addition to the boon limit.<br /> <br /> If the devs took the Fate approach for making Fate Fractal and Stunts, or the Cortex Prime approach for Triggers, explaining in the book what is the mechanical and narrative possibility of every dot for any relic, it would be far easier for a Storyguide to adjudicate things, even weirder things players would want, and even what is the power level expected of the campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23839-oxcelot","user":"Oxcelot","date":". 06-06-2020, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23839-oxcelot","name":"Oxcelot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T21:15:31-07:00","id":1395227,"title":"","content":"There is no text suggesting that it needs a purview first. This means that if you have a magic carpet, it might be able to fly but not able to grant control of all wind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T21:22:11-07:00","id":1395228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1395227#post1395227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no text suggesting that it needs a purview first. This means that if you have a magic carpet, it might be able to fly but not able to grant control of all wind.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s exactly the point here! Thanks!<br /> <br /> Being lengendary doesn\u2019t mean versatile or powerful, just means it has special powers, like my sword that cuts a portal on reality, but can\u2019t allow me to see from the stars point of view or anything like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T22:51:03-07:00","id":1395247,"title":"","content":"The more forum posts I read, the more it seems apparent that we desperately need a clearly-written set of examples on how to write up a character, create an artifact, choose and use boons/miracles, etc, apply skills in-game, run a combat, and advance from mortal to hero. Time and again, there are examples from STs and players of confusion, frustration, and misinterpretation of rules, and this can all be cleared up by the devs putting out a short, free book of examples and walk-throughs for us to see exactly what they intend. It shouldn't be this way (it really should be clear in the books), but obviously, help is needed. Agreed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T23:31:26-07:00","id":1395253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1395247#post1395247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more forum posts I read, the more it seems apparent that we desperately need a clearly-written set of examples on how to write up a character, create an artifact, choose and use boons/miracles, etc, apply skills in-game, run a combat, and advance from mortal to hero. Time and again, there are examples from STs and players of confusion, frustration, and misinterpretation of rules, and this can all be cleared up by the devs putting out a short, free book of examples and walk-throughs for us to see exactly what they intend. It shouldn't be this way (it really should be clear in the books), but obviously, help is needed. Agreed?</div> </div> </div> </div>The confusion here is from a book that's going through its last round of errata. I find the examples in the corebook just fine, and I'm submitting feedback on these features of a book that's still in development so that when it gets released for general consumption it will be clearer. I find that the two books we have so far worked well enough and I was able to help my players figure it out. When to use Skills, how to make a character, when to use Boons or Marvels, upgrading a Hero, running combat, I never had a problem with those.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually maybe I should make a Big Book Of Examples and throw it on the Nexus for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 06-09-2020, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T05:22:38-07:00","id":1395313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1395253#post1395253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Actually maybe I should make a Big Book Of Examples and throw it on the Nexus for free.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would support this. Even with paying small fee for this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T06:34:23-07:00","id":1395332,"title":"","content":"\u201cpay what you want\u201d rather than \u201cfree\u201d, perhaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T00:05:43-07:00","id":1395535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1395332#post1395332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cpay what you want\u201d rather than \u201cfree\u201d, perhaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm working on something I DO plan on charging money for but I wouldn't feel right asking money for a project that's going to be 90% &quot;So by looking at Page X we see it's something like [Example Block]&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T09:54:21-07:00","id":1395614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1395535#post1395535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm working on something I DO plan on charging money for but I wouldn't feel right asking money for a project that's going to be 90% &amp;quot;So by looking at Page X we see it's something like [Example Block]&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>People routinely charged for the book &quot;The Long Lost Friend&quot; AKA &quot;Pow Wows,&quot; and it's mainly which Bible verse to read for what occult power you want to harness. Look it up on Wikipedia, it's a real book . It has an amazingly sinister reputation and gets into horror stories as a backwoods Necronomicon, but it's real and mainly lists of Bible verses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T11:44:09-07:00","id":1395633,"title":"","content":"Maybe \u201cpay what you want\u201d with the suggested price being $0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T13:08:45-07:00","id":1395656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1395614#post1395614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People routinely charged for the book &quot;The Long Lost Friend&quot; AKA &quot;Pow Wows,&quot; and it's mainly which Bible verse to read for what occult power you want to harness. Look it up on Wikipedia, it's a real book . It has an amazingly sinister reputation and gets into horror stories as a backwoods Necronomicon, but it's real and mainly lists of Bible verses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well good for them, but I'm not them. Plus it feels a little scummy to be asking for money on the Storypath Nexus when my product touches so heavily on the mechanics that will be in the main books.<br /> <br /> Honestly, having slept on it, I'll probably just make it a thread on this forum, full of examples, my personal rule interpretations, and maybe taking some open questions for things like &quot;So how do you do Stealth?&quot;<br /> <br /> (Answer: Don't make it a roll-off if you don't have to, such as Chases or Contests. It's less of a pain if you say &quot;Okay it's Difficulty 2 to sneak past the cyclops since you blinded him, get Enhancement for your doofy goat plan&quot; or &quot;Can you give me an Empathy and Mental roll? Difficulty 3. Okay, yeah, you notice that the assistant is palming a knife. Roll Close Combat and let's say Mental to try and stop him before he stabs your boss.&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 06-10-2020, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T20:14:43-07:00","id":1395738,"title":"","content":"Where did it say or imply that the 1 dot \u201cadd a boon to my relic\u201d boon cost the price of doing it as a marvel? I saw nothing remotely suggesting it was anything other than using the boon out of the book as if you bought it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T09:31:33-07:00","id":1396184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/317296/A-Pain-in-the-Dice-Guide-to-Scion-Character-Creation\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/317296.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/317296/A-Pain-in-the-Dice-Guide-to-Scion-Character-Creation\" target=\"_blank\"> A Pain in the Dice Guide to Scion Character Creation - Onyx Path Publishing | StoryPath Nexus | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/317296/A-Pain-in-the-Dice-Guide-to-Scion-Character-Creation\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/317296/A-Pain-in-the-Dice-Guide-to-Scion-Character-Creation </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A Pain in the Dice Guide to Scion Character Creation - Scion 2nd Edition character creation can be a challenge with details spread across multiple books, especially for new pl </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Didn't buy yet, but looks like its an interesting work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T10:48:52-07:00","id":1396193,"title":"","content":"So is anyone who has the book willing to namedrop the Loa, Yazatas, and Nementondevos featured in the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T11:59:44-07:00","id":1396198,"title":"","content":"Legba, The Barons (there are at least 3, Cemitiere, La Croix and Samedi), Dambala, Ezili, Kalfu, Lsyren and Ogou, also Azaka, Marassa Dosu Dosa, Assange and Sabata are identical to the Orisha mantle.<br /> <br /> Andarta, Belenos, Cernunnos, Epona, Esos, Nantosuelta, Nehalennia, Taris and Sulis.<br /> <br /> Anahita, Ashi, Atar, Haoma, Hvare-Khshaeta, Mangha, Mithra, Rashnu, Sraosha, Tishtrya, Vanant, Vata-Vayu, Verethragna and Zan<br /> <br /> A few extras: Bragi, Vishvakarman, Omoikane, Biboonike, Upuat, Erinle, Doumu, Xolotl, Hecate, Midir and Columbia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T12:06:21-07:00","id":1396199,"title":"","content":"Thank you Mateus! That's a really interesting list!<br /> <br /> Edit: Okay, I guess I'll leave my thoughts.<br /> <br /> The Loa: That's a good list. I'm pleased that the Barons are a group of deities rather than a single one this time around. I would honestly have liked to see Ezili handled the same way though, and I am a little disappointed not to see Maman Brigitte. Oh well. She shouldn't be too hard to homebrew, though.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Nemetondevos: Seems like a good list. I know a lot of what I think I know about these guys is based on outdated information, however, so I'm really interested in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a>'s opinion, if they have the book. Is Cernunnos at the very least a deity of commerce and not of the hunt? I'm glad to see that &quot;Teutates&quot; isn't on there, as that term gets applied to a single Gaulish god way too often.<br /> <br /> Yazatas: Honestly, I don't really know enough about the Yazatas to have an opinion. I have read the 1e write-up of them, but given that as Samudra put it, actual practitioners of Zoroastrianconsider it to be so bad as to be heretical even when the religion doesn't have a concept of heresy, I think it would be best if I just assumed I lack knowledge of them completely. That being said, the fact that there's fourteen of them is cool, as it means all the big ones are probably covered at least.<br /> <br /> As for the miscellaneous deities, it's an interesting list with a few I didn't honestly expect. Hecate was definitely the obvious choice for the Theoi, but beyond that I'm surprised by most of them. I really would have put my money on Ganga for the Deva, for instance. Not that there's anything wrong with Samudra's homebrew write-up and I'll happily use it, but I more or less assumed she was the most important one not yet present. Upuat would not have been my first guess for the Netjer, either, though to be honest I can easily name two dozen Netjer I'd like to see thrown in and would have been happy with any of them. Thanks to my Egypt phase. You know, we all had one.<br /> <br /> Very pleasantly surprised to see Xolotl. He's a personal favorite of mine, and I'd honestly love to play a Scion of him at some point. I'm really interested in playing a Teotl scion, and Xolotl would be a really intriguing choice, being a protector of the deformed, disabled, and generally ostracized. Plus he looks so damn cool and I'd love to have my character get gradually more monstrous as their legend increases, and he seems like a good patron for that idea.<br /> <br /> I take it Columbia is either unaligned or a spun-off Theoi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","user":"Wannabe Demon Lord","date":". 06-13-2020, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T15:47:41-07:00","id":1396226,"title":"","content":"Columbia is unaligned, but she is a Scion of Athena and have many friend among the Theoi (her sisters and cousins). She actually have no access to the Metamorphosis Purview, as far as I understand.<br /> <br /> On Cernunnos, I think they discovered lots of stuff recently about its cult, but I definitely can't be used as reference here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T16:12:33-07:00","id":1396232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1396199#post1396199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Cernunnos at the very least a deity of commerce and not of the hunt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Callings do not include Hunter, and one of his purviews is Prosperity. The write-up focuses on wealth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T16:17:27-07:00","id":1396237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1396199#post1396199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take it Columbia is either unaligned or a spun-off Theoi?</div> </div> </div> </div>She gets along with the Theoi well enough that she shares a Mantle with the pantheon as the Goddess Libertas. She gets roughly two pages in the book and serves as examples both of how to make your character the Scion of a god who isn't part of a pantheon and therefore provides no PSP, and how you could go about making a national god for a modern country. Being a Scion of Columbia or other non-pantheon god actually sounds rather nice; my character could literally take nerd culture as their 'chosen people' and get social bonuses involving nerds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 06-13-2020, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T17:17:13-07:00","id":1396249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1396237#post1396237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She gets along with the Theoi well enough that she shares a Mantle with the pantheon as the Goddess Libertas. She gets roughly two pages in the book and serves as examples both of how to make your character the Scion of a god who isn't part of a pantheon and therefore provides no PSP, and how you could go about making a national god for a modern country. Being a Scion of Columbia or other non-pantheon god actually sounds rather nice; my character could literally take nerd culture as their 'chosen people' and get social bonuses involving nerds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much like the new gods in American Gods. It's an interesting door opening, gods without Pantheon, but with powers coming from their communities (worshipers, in a certain way). Worth a future discussion once the book is released and we can all discuss it on the same level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T17:27:04-07:00","id":1396253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1396249#post1396249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Much like the new gods in American Gods. It's an interesting door opening, gods without Pantheon, but with powers coming from their communities (worshipers, in a certain way). Worth a future discussion once the book is released and we can all discuss it on the same level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean their power comes from their Legends and Deeds, much like Gods <i>with</i> a Pantheon. It's just that some of them form a Covenant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T17:31:00-07:00","id":1396255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1396253#post1396253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean their power comes from their Legends and Deeds, much like Gods <i>with</i> a Pantheon. It's just that some of them form a Covenant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure the power comes from the gods and their legend, but what I mean is, like the purview comes from the Guide or the Relic, it comes from the Covenant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T17:52:31-07:00","id":1396264,"title":"","content":"A Covenant Hero might gain a Motif and maybe some Knacks or Boon access through their Covenant if they don't have a Pantheon, but I try to avoid any and all attempts to tie &quot;Gods get their power from Prayer and Belief in them&quot; in Scion. Because they don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T22:07:27-07:00","id":1396314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1396199#post1396199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe Nemetondevos: Seems like a good list. I know a lot of what I think I know about these guys is based on outdated information, however, so I'm really interested in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a>'s opinion, if they have the book. Is Cernunnos at the very least a deity of commerce and not of the hunt? I'm glad to see that &quot;Teutates&quot; isn't on there, as that term gets applied to a single Gaulish god way too often.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the moment I am waiting for Companion to be available to everyone before I go into details about it, and I'll probably give a little talk or something in the Scion Fan Discord just for sake of ease. So, if people want to check that out, it'll happen there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T08:32:59-07:00","id":1396877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1394483#post1394483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See this is why I'd flat-out ban putting Boons on Relics. It just feels like it's trying to game the system. You want to do Marvels through a Relic? Put Purviews on it and make a Marvel with it. And if it's just &quot;Get a Boon from a different Purview&quot; for one dot then especially banned, because there's no way I'm letting Boons cost less than a flipping Knack.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've always charged boons as 2 dots - very slightly modified - and they cost the legend as though they'd been marveled. This was based off of the Icarian Wings. It allows 24 hours of flight (pretty sure, book's not on hand) for spending 1 legend (as though you had marveled the sky boon). In this way you can add unique gifts to items that you don't necessarily want to give access to a purview - such as a teleporting sword or a flying boat. But based on other relics I still think it should be 2 dots, and charge the legend of a marvel. So that teleporting sword? 2 legend to teleport with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24323-zipdrive","name":"ZipDrive","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T08:52:03-07:00","id":1396884,"title":"","content":"I was checking the relics in Hero, and there is at least one example of a boom granted that is pretty obvious, Icarean Wings.<br /> <br /> It gives access to Flight (the Sky purview boom) as a Knack, with the cost of a Marvel (the cost is Imbue a legend, And the relic requires to spend a legend).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T11:43:10-07:00","id":1396906,"title":"","content":"I don't mind a Motif-free Marvel at Marvel Prices on a Relic, I just don't like putting Boons on Relics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T12:40:44-07:00","id":1396919,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not totally convinced Covenant is worth the investment for a Scion with a Pantheon, at least not at the lower levels. I might rule that it provides a bonus Title to evoke in your role as protector of the given community","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T12:45:12-07:00","id":1396920,"title":"","content":"Reading it I had the same feeling.<br /> <br /> The extra title will hardly be much different from any of your other titles to the point to be used when none of the others can be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T19:05:31-07:00","id":1407418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1396198#post1396198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legba, The Barons (there are at least 3, Cemitiere, La Croix and Samedi), Dambala, Ezili, Kalfu, Lsyren and Ogou, also Azaka, Marassa Dosu Dosa, Assange and Sabata are identical to the Orisha mantle.<br /> <br /> Andarta, Belenos, Cernunnos, Epona, Esos, Nantosuelta, Nehalennia, Taris and Sulis.<br /> <br /> Anahita, Ashi, Atar, Haoma, Hvare-Khshaeta, Mangha, Mithra, Rashnu, Sraosha, Tishtrya, Vanant, Vata-Vayu, Verethragna and Zan<br /> <br /> A few extras: Bragi, Vishvakarman, Omoikane, Biboonike, Upuat, Erinle, Doumu, Xolotl, Hecate, Midir and Columbia.</div> </div> </div> </div>The recent update has altered this list, (which already excluded new Mantles of deities for the new pantheons). Notably, it has dropped Columbia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T20:43:46-07:00","id":1407440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1407418#post1407418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Notably, it has dropped Columbia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Neall said in a podcast that they felt like they needed more than just a single entry in the Companion to address the ins and outs of Columbia's past, and that especially given all happening now they felt like they'd need more time and words to do her right.<br /> <br /> Which is entirely fair, IMO","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T22:11:31-07:00","id":1407446,"title":"","content":"Any word if someone else is filling of the niche of &quot;example of pantheonless deity with a Covenant-path?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T23:06:11-07:00","id":1407449,"title":"","content":"From a quick look at the latest version, there's no sample God that has Covenant, just the Birthright and a sidebar describing how it's often used by Gods with no Pantheons, and some advice on generating Motifs and Virtues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T23:20:47-07:00","id":1407450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1407449#post1407449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a quick look at the latest version, there's no sample God that has Covenant, just the Birthright and a sidebar describing how it's often used by Gods with no Pantheons, and some advice on generating Motifs and Virtues.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh is it the updated version available to redownload by backers? I missed that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T03:46:35-07:00","id":1407478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1407418#post1407418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The recent update has altered this list, (which already excluded new Mantles of deities for the new pantheons). Notably, it has dropped Columbia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dropped Columbia! That wounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T09:35:47-07:00","id":1407536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1407478#post1407478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dropped Columbia! That wounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Symbol of Manifest Destiny needs way more attention to get her right rather than hand waving everything bad that is inseparable from the concept of America as people misusing her image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-11-2020, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T11:18:09-07:00","id":1407557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1407478#post1407478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dropped Columbia! That wounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoting myself here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, Neall said in a podcast that they felt like they needed more than just a single entry in the Companion to address the ins and outs of Columbia's past, and that especially given all happening now they felt like they'd need more time and words to do her right.<br /> <br /> Which is entirely fair, IMO </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T17:50:27-07:00","id":1407825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1407536#post1407536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Symbol of Manifest Destiny needs way more attention to get her right rather than hand waving everything bad that is inseparable from the concept of America as people misusing her image.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The symbols of other nations can be seen as being a manifestation of the nobility and virtues of that nation. American symbols all seem to be equated with swastikas and other symbols of evil. It feels like the USA is always depicted as a force of unlimited evil across all of this company's games. The only unambiguous depictions of positive traits linked to America by this company date from the 1990s. It gets tiresome and looks like a failure of creativity and fairness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-12-2020, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T18:28:19-07:00","id":1407831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1407825#post1407825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The symbols of other nations can be seen as being a manifestation of the nobility and virtues of that nation. American symbols all seem to be equated with swastikas and other symbols of evil. It feels like the USA is always depicted as a force of unlimited evil across all of this company's games. The only unambiguous depictions of positive traits linked to America by this company date from the 1990s. It gets tiresome and looks like a failure of creativity and fairness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are no symbols of modern nationalism that are treated as gods yet in Scion 2E, so I don't know what comparison you are drawing. If you are referring to the 1E pantheons, those were awful too.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it is a failure of creativity and downright act of white washing genocide to talk about Columbia and exclude exactly how that symbol has been used historically. Her use is her only existence, after all she has no other &quot;lore&quot; for that use to contradict. It's not like Jesus where we can say &quot;Yes atrocities have been committed in His name, but we have His words in His narrative, and can see how these acts defy His actual story and teachings.&quot; The symbolic usage of Columbia is literally all we have to go on, and that writeup ignored it.<br /> <br /> This is Columbia: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Columbia_(personification)#/media/File:American_Progress_(John_Gast_painting).jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Columb..._painting).jpg</a><br /> <br /> If a writeup pretends that THAT^ is not Columbia, it is a bad writeup. It can't just be some separate bad Mantle either, since &quot;America&quot; as a place where the good stuff can exist only gets to occupy space because of THAT^.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T19:13:33-07:00","id":1407844,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s always important to remember that Columbia literally started as a propaganda piece to justify Manifest Destiny, the idea that caused so many of USA\u2019s more horrible crimes against Native peoples. Afterwards? She was basically nonexistent, there are plenty of other figures to use as divine patrons of America","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T19:49:05-07:00","id":1407848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1407844#post1407844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s always important to remember that Columbia literally started as a propaganda piece to justify Manifest Destiny, the idea that caused so many of USA\u2019s more horrible crimes against Native peoples. Afterwards? She was basically nonexistent, there are plenty of other figures to use as divine patrons of America</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't say &quot;started&quot;, but that was certainly her peak. Her first known personification with that name precisely was in Phillis Wheatley's poetry in 1776, unsurprisingly in the context of liberty vs British tyranny. And descending from Wheatley's usage (Wheatley herself being Black), Columbia got some strong usage among abolitionists, to the point that Columbia/Liberty in the Phygrian Cap was politically banned symbol in Southern papers in the 19th Century.<br /> <br /> But yes without a doubt, her most predominant mainstream usage in American iconography is as the embodiment of Manifest Destiny. And she largely disappears afterward UNLESS you conflate her with Lady Liberty (ala the statue), which is a valid take.<br /> <br /> In short I'd portray Columbia as having been on the right side of history of slavery and immigration, but unspeakably blood soaked on Westward expansion, and US imperialism in Latin America, and not on speaking terms with the Native Pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-12-2020, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T20:45:59-07:00","id":1407857,"title":"","content":"Ahh my mistake","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T02:46:51-07:00","id":1407880,"title":"","content":"Columbia is still around, she got a gig in comic books. She shortened her gown to kulats and got herself a magic lasso and an invisible plane. Uncle Sam went the same route as did Hercules, Venus, and Thor, heck even Loki is doing the same thing these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T07:12:52-07:00","id":1407927,"title":"","content":"So, I'm just going to put myself here for better or worse.<br /> <br /> I wrote up Columbia for the Additional Gods section over two years ago. It wasn't an entry I was expecting to write, and the one that I struggled the most with because I was very much aware of Columbia's history as a personification of Manifest Destiny and the role that it played in the subjugation of non-white European-descended Americans. Trying to find and then striking a good balance on my first foray into writing for Scion 2E was <i>extremely </i><i>difficult</i>, because I wanted to handle it with as much care while also allowing Columbia to be an example of how a god/dess/dex can overcome how their previous mythos was abused by opportunists, and then making the conscious decision by turning it around and becoming a wholly new symbol unto herself. It's also part of why in the &quot;ancient&quot; illustration spread, she is shown as we've known her in media (see: the Columbia Pictures mascot, a white woman) and why in the &quot;modern&quot; illustration spread she is a woman of color.<br /> <br /> Between the time Columbia was written up and then going to proofing/press, it was clear to the developers that Columbia required a much larger, thoughtful, and more nuanced write up that you simply could not fit into a 500 word-per-entry budget. I stand by them in this decision, and hope that if/when/ever the opportunity arises for Columbia to appear in a 2E supplement, that she is given that nuanced write up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.erykahfassett.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman, serif\"><b>Erykah Fassett</b></span></a><br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;The closer you get to the light, the greater your shadow becomes.&quot;</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24398-shadowblossoms","name":"ShadowBlossoms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24398_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T10:12:04-07:00","id":1407970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1407880#post1407880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Columbia is still around, she got a gig in comic books. She shortened her gown to kulats and got herself a magic lasso and an invisible plane. Uncle Sam went the same route as did Hercules, Venus, and Thor, heck even Loki is doing the same thing these days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excuse me, but the fuck? Where the shit did you get this concept that Columbia, America's Ego made manifest, was Wonder Woman, a literal Amazon, of Grecian legend? A big chunk of her whole thing is that she is an Immigrant, same with Superman.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T10:13:45-07:00","id":1407971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1407880#post1407880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Columbia is still around, she got a gig in comic books. She shortened her gown to kulats and got herself a magic lasso and an invisible plane. Uncle Sam went the same route as did Hercules, Venus, and Thor, heck even Loki is doing the same thing these days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you put some more detail please? How is Columbia tied to Wonder Woman, and what do you mean by Uncle Sam going the same route as Hercules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T10:45:56-07:00","id":1407983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowBlossoms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1407927#post1407927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm just going to put myself here for better or worse.<br /> <br /> I wrote up Columbia for the Additional Gods section over two years ago. It wasn't an entry I was expecting to write, and the one that I struggled the most with because I was very much aware of Columbia's history as a personification of Manifest Destiny and the role that it played in the subjugation of non-white European-descended Americans. Trying to find and then striking a good balance on my first foray into writing for Scion 2E was <i>extremely </i><i>difficult</i>, because I wanted to handle it with as much care while also allowing Columbia to be an example of how a god/dess/dex can overcome how their previous mythos was abused by opportunists, and then making the conscious decision by turning it around and becoming a wholly new symbol unto herself. It's also part of why in the &amp;quot;ancient&amp;quot; illustration spread, she is shown as we've known her in media (see: the Columbia Pictures mascot, a white woman) and why in the &amp;quot;modern&amp;quot; illustration spread she is a woman of color.<br /> <br /> Between the time Columbia was written up and then going to proofing/press, it was clear to the developers that Columbia required a much larger, thoughtful, and more nuanced write up that you simply could not fit into a 500 word-per-entry budget. I stand by them in this decision, and hope that if/when/ever the opportunity arises for Columbia to appear in a 2E supplement, that she is given that nuanced write up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for explaining about Columbia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T10:50:02-07:00","id":1407985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1407831#post1407831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There are no symbols of modern nationalism that are treated as gods yet in Scion 2E, so I don't know what comparison you are drawing. If you are referring to the 1E pantheons, those were awful too.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it is a failure of creativity and downright act of white washing genocide to talk about Columbia and exclude exactly how that symbol has been used historically. Her use is her only existence, after all she has no other &amp;quot;lore&amp;quot; for that use to contradict. It's not like Jesus where we can say &amp;quot;Yes atrocities have been committed in His name, but we have His words in His narrative, and can see how these acts defy His actual story and teachings.&amp;quot; The symbolic usage of Columbia is literally all we have to go on, and that writeup ignored it.<br /> <br /> This is Columbia: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Columbia_(personification)#/media/File:American_Progress_(John_Gast_painting).jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Columb..._painting).jpg</a><br /> <br /> If a writeup pretends that THAT^ is not Columbia, it is a bad writeup. It can't just be some separate bad Mantle either, since &amp;quot;America&amp;quot; as a place where the good stuff can exist only gets to occupy space because of THAT^.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with your analysis. And I didn\u2019t know about all the historical stuff in your second post. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T11:34:21-07:00","id":1407992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1407971#post1407971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you put some more detail please? How is Columbia tied to Wonder Woman, and what do you mean by Uncle Sam going the same route as Hercules?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wonder Woman has the same costume as Columbia, the skirt was made shorter and then changed to a bathing suit bottom. Wonder Woman also has the same hair that newspaper cartoonists gave Columbia. In the 1940's Uncle Sam was a superhero over at Quality comics ( they also did Plastic Man and the Blackhawks). Hercules and Venus were both superheroes in Atlas Timely comics in the 1940s. Thor has been a Superhero for Marvel since the 1960s. Loki and Isis have been superheroes for Marvel and DC respectively in this decade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T13:03:41-07:00","id":1408004,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t see Wonder Woman as Columbia, while the aspect of her as a immigrant apply to Columbia too (she is pretty white and blonde, not very Native American). I think the most Columbia superhero is Captain America, he is a warrior defending freedom at the cost of \u201cevil people\u201d (Native American, Germans, Japanese, Soviets, whoever is the enemy of the people).<br /> <br /> Of course he is a man, not a woman, that is part of the archetype desired, Columbia had to be defended by you, the men, the soldiers, she is a maid in danger, an inspiration, while Cap is the hero, the other side of the coin, you don\u2019t need to defend him, but you need to help him to achieve.<br /> <br /> He is the evolution of America self image, not the maid getting free from tyrants and shackles, but the soldier that brings freedom with him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T13:03:43-07:00","id":1408005,"title":"","content":"I gotta say, that going &quot;She dresses a LITTLE like Columbia&quot; isn't a very compelling &quot;No she totally IS Columbia&quot; case","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T13:08:39-07:00","id":1408007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408004#post1408004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course he is a man, not a woman, that is part of the archetype desired, Columbia had to be defended by you, the men, the soldiers, she is a maid in danger, an inspiration, while Cap is the hero, the other side of the coin, you don\u2019t need to defend him, but you need to help him to achieve.<br /> <br /> He is the evolution of America self image, not the maid getting free from tyrants and shackles, but the soldier that brings freedom with him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uncle Sam is/was considered a mantle spin-off of Columbia. So, if anything, Steve Rogers could be wearing that mantle for a hot minute (at least during WW2).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.erykahfassett.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman, serif\"><b>Erykah Fassett</b></span></a><br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;The closer you get to the light, the greater your shadow becomes.&quot;</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24398-shadowblossoms","name":"ShadowBlossoms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24398_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T14:00:49-07:00","id":1408019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowBlossoms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408007#post1408007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uncle Sam is/was considered a mantle spin-off of Columbia.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s interesting, I didn\u2019t know that, but it\u2019s pretty much obvious, both were the personification of America asking for help for a national effort, Columbia for the expansion effort and Uncle Sam for the war effort.<br /> <br /> A personal note on Uncle Sam, when I see his image, I see the image of a more evil USA: that rich old man asking for you to fight his war.<br /> He is like the Monopoly guy, he dress in a very fancy way (high top hat, smoking, etc) and at same time not fancy at all (it\u2019s all colorful, even being USA colors, it\u2019s not the standard black tie), that points he is rich enough to make a joke with expensive clothes (while others can\u2019t afford a single suit, he have enough to buy one that he would never use in public). He is there pointing to you with an angry face, as if it was your fault and saying \u201cthat your problem go deal with it\u201d, even when you had nothing to do with it.<br /> Well, he is not my country war symbol, so I can\u2019t judge. (my country symbol was a Snake smoking a pipe, what is a kind of a joke with an old expression for things are going bad...).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T15:38:53-07:00","id":1408050,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24398-shadowblossoms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24398_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24398\" data-vbnamecard=\"24398\">ShadowBlossoms</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz I Liked both your posts about Uncle Sam.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a> I could be wrong, but I think you\u2019re being too literal in your interpretation of Columbia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T15:40:09-07:00","id":1408051,"title":"","content":"I can\u2019t wait to read this book! Might even give up Netflix and chill for it lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T15:53:15-07:00","id":1408056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1407992#post1407992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wonder Woman has the same costume as Columbia, the skirt was made shorter and then changed to a bathing suit bottom. Wonder Woman also has the same hair that newspaper cartoonists gave Columbia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wonder Woman was written by a radical feminist to harness the idea of the mythic Amazons to depict and promote his world view that a world governed by women would be a kinder, fairer place and that men would find their greater happiness and fulfilment in voluntary interpersonal submission to them.<br /> <br /> Hence the lasso (i.e. &quot;you have no idea how much you'll get off from being tied up&quot;).<br /> <br /> There might be an incidental visual commonality, but an assertion that the character is intended as a depiction of a national personification seems like a fairly shallow reading.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T16:31:46-07:00","id":1408066,"title":"","content":"But Morton made it clear that he drew on the image of Columbia and meant to make Wonder Woman a new iteration of Miss Columbia from the newspaper political cartoons. He said she was the female Uncle Sam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T16:58:05-07:00","id":1408073,"title":"","content":"I knew Wonder Woman was supposed to be a feminist icon. Idk she was actually dom. One person told me the opposite, how in a lot of the old 1940s stories she gets tied up by her own magic lasso.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T17:17:28-07:00","id":1408076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408066#post1408066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Morton made it clear that he drew on the image of Columbia and meant to make Wonder Woman a new iteration of Miss Columbia from the newspaper political cartoons. He said she was the female Uncle Sam.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so I had to look this up and all I can find is one source claiming that the artist who did the original design of Wonder Woman was friends with an artist who did illustrations of Uncle Sam and Columbia, and a whole bunch of unrelated articles going ga-ga over Columbia and comparing her to Wonder Woman (which is not in any way compelling proof), so:<br /> <br /> A. Please provide a source for that, and<br /> <br /> B. Explain how <i>additional history</i> in any way counters the writers' worries that a 500 word write up wasn't enough to properly tackle Columbia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T17:36:34-07:00","id":1408079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408073#post1408073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I knew Wonder Woman was supposed to be a feminist icon. Idk she was actually dom. One person told me the opposite, how in a lot of the old 1940s stories she gets tied up by her own magic lasso.</div> </div> </div> </div>She would be bound by figures attempting to confine her for the purposes of inevitably breaking free.<br /> <br /> She would conversely bind others, for the purposes of liberating them. There was a back and forth to it.<br /> <br /> Also it would have been kind of titillating, but in a manner that was still challenging to the mores of the day.<br /> <br /> (Character's creator was also in a poly relationship)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T18:14:31-07:00","id":1408085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408076#post1408076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, so I had to look this up and all I can find is one source claiming that the artist who did the original design of Wonder Woman was friends with an artist who did illustrations of Uncle Sam and Columbia, and a whole bunch of unrelated articles going ga-ga over Columbia and comparing her to Wonder Woman (which is not in any way compelling proof), so:<br /> <br /> A. Please provide a source for that, and<br /> <br /> B. Explain how <i>additional history</i> in any way counters the writers' worries that a 500 word write up wasn't enough to properly tackle Columbia?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was a side issue that came up in an interdisciplinary course on Political Cartoons and their major tropes and means of communication I took in college back in the 1980s. So I no longer have the books with the references. Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T19:36:13-07:00","id":1408092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408085#post1408085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a side issue that came up in an interdisciplinary course on Political Cartoons and their major tropes and means of communication I took in college back in the 1980s. So I no longer have the books with the references. Sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless, it's still far less than enough to argue away the inherent problems of Columbia as a symbol for Manifest Destiny. Going purely &quot;Ra-ra USA!&quot; ignores the simple fact that America isn't the Shining City on a Hill that it made itself out to be, particularly for some of the Pantheons that feature in the game already. (Such as the Manitou and the Orisha).<br /> <br /> Also just giving America a patron Goddess, based on a figure that was never worshiped by anyone and was really never more than a visualized personification in paintings and political cartoons, is already pretty weird, regardless of how she's portrayed. (Same with Uncle Sam)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","name":"Ravian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T00:25:33-07:00","id":1408112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408092#post1408092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Regardless, it's still far less than enough to argue away the inherent problems of Columbia as a symbol for Manifest Destiny. Going purely &amp;quot;Ra-ra USA!&amp;quot; ignores the simple fact that America isn't the Shining City on a Hill that it made itself out to be, particularly for some of the Pantheons that feature in the game already. (Such as the Manitou and the Orisha).<br /> <br /> Also just giving America a patron Goddess, based on a figure that was never worshiped by anyone and was really never more than a visualized personification in paintings and political cartoons, is already pretty weird, regardless of how she's portrayed. (Same with Uncle Sam)</div> </div> </div> </div>Uncle Sam I agree (notably an unusual national symbol in his own right as he represents the GOVERNMENT more than anything else), but Columbia is pretty directly modeled on tutelary deities, down to the faux-Roman name, and spoken of historically in deific terms. She wasn\u2019t literally worshipped because the people using her iconography were largely monotheists, but in the World, where European polytheism never stopped being practiced it stands to reason she\u2019d translate directly to tutelary goddess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T02:54:44-07:00","id":1408119,"title":"","content":"This book is really good, especially the parts about setting the dials in your campaign and the new pantheons. And the part about converting from 1e to 2e would probably be really useful if you have a preexisting 1e campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T04:57:28-07:00","id":1408126,"title":"","content":"Before the tangent were my joke about Gods getting gigs as comic book superheroes was taken way too seriously we were discussing why American symbol and the USA is demonized around here. <br /> <br /> We have pantheons in this game presented as pure and noble in virtue that mandated slavery, genocide, human sacrafise by torture, and worse. Compared to many admired pantheons and deities (and living faiths still practiced) the USA at its worst still looks better even noble. Let's remember that, if you look back far enough, every nation exists because it destroyed other peoples. <br /> <br /> Take China for example. Archeology proves that the area that would become China had a diversity of peoples that makes the five hundred nations of North America seem paltry. These peoples are gone. They were wiped out. They left no trace in the Chinese language, and the Han Chinese have no genetic traces of these peoples in their population. I chose China as the extreme example, but there are many similar examples planetwide. Meanwhile, the USA has substantial Native American populations, programs to preserve Native American languages and cultures, and active reform movements to ameliorate continuing abuses. Many nations deny they even had a history before the present population's arrival and ascendency. America always acknowledged the truth. As an American who can point to ancestry from at least three Native American nations, let me point out that there was intermarriage and minglings of populations. <br /> <br /> America is not alone as an exception, both Canada and New Zealand did better, but to paint America as an exceptional force of evil is simply wrong and corrupt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T05:18:15-07:00","id":1408128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408126#post1408126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before the tangent were my joke about Gods getting gigs as comic book superheroes was taken way too seriously we were discussing why American symbol and the USA is demonized around here</div> </div> </div> </div>... which itself was a tangent. The person who <i>actually wrote the Columbia section</i> explained why it was removed, and is the one person you've decided not to engage with at all, so this is no longer about the Companion, is it?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T05:35:25-07:00","id":1408133,"title":"","content":"I for one am quite happy with the entry she got in the Nexus product dealing with the American founders and the Theoi (\u201cGods of the Republic\u201d, I think it was called?). If she never appears in an official Scion product beyond the brief mentions she's already received, that will be fine with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T05:36:05-07:00","id":1408134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408126#post1408126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the USA at its worst still looks better even noble</div> </div> </div> </div>That is one hell of a claim to make less than a week after the anniversary of the Hiroshima and Nagasaki bombings and while there are ongoing human rights violations declared as such by international organisations both in the actions of the US National Guard against the BLM protesters and in the concentration camps set up for immigrants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Take China for example. Archeology proves that the area that would become China had a diversity of peoples that makes the five hundred nations of North America seem paltry. These peoples are gone. They were wiped out. </div> </div> </div>Do you have any evidence of these claims? Like, I'm not going to paint China, which is currently enacting a genocide (Uyghurs) and violating international treaties just to curb free speech (Hongkong), not to mention their everyday abuses, as an in any way legitimate regime. But I've never heard of this massive genocide you are speaking of, one that would have had to take place some time in the Stone Age (and then, it would be very hard to prove those other ethnicities were systematically killed) to fit into what I learned in the way of Chinese archaeological chronology. Historically, we have ample evidence of how the multi-ethnic, multi-religious make-up that defines China today came about. And there was absolutely colonialism and genocide involved there, particularly along the southern borders, and that should be addressed more. These historical events don't obscure either the horrors China perpetrates today, nor those the US does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> America always acknowledged the truth. </div> </div> </div>Are Thanksgiving celebrations that erase the violence enacted by the Pilgrims against the very nations that helped them an acknowledgement of the truth (<a href=\"https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2019/11/25/the-invention-of-thanksgiving)?\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2...thanksgiving)?</a> Are school books that teach children that enslaved Africans were no more than &quot;immigrant workers&quot; acknowledging the truth (<a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2015/10/06/us/publisher-promises-revisions-after-textbook-refers-to-african-slaves-as-workers.html)?\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.nytimes.com/2015/10/06/u...workers.html)?</a> I'm sorry, but this is plain historical whitewashing. No one says that other countries don't share the US's dismal historical record (though few can rival its present negative impact, just think of the Iraq War). The problem lies <i>precisely</i> in a continued <i>lack</i> of acknowledgement, and in a continuation of the injustice founded in colonial times. As federal bodies withhold aid from Native tribes, as reservations are kept food deserts and often lack clean water, as reservations and whole tribes are legally dissolved because of business interests, as police violence against Black Americans and the prison industry attached to it continue a legacy of racism, segregation, and enslavement, the truth of history is <i>not</i> acknlowledged, but tacitly continued as a reign of injustice in the present. And <i>that</i> is why the writers of this game have decided to take more time and wordcount for Columbia - she isn't cut, you won't have to live without the fully fictional deification of your national symbol - the only such, at that, in a game that is otherwise about real-world religions. You'll just have to wait while people take the time to address some sensitive issues. And if you see that as unjustified demonisation of your country already, I think you really need to examine the stance you take both to your country and to the entertainment you consume.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","user":"Sacerdos","date":".  Added source links I forgot to post the first time around 08-14-2020, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T06:16:11-07:00","id":1408139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408126#post1408126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compared to many admired pantheons and deities (and living faiths still practiced) the USA at its worst still looks better even noble.</div> </div> </div> </div>The USA is neither a Pantheon nor a Deity, so the comparison makes no sense... where is this mysterious lionization of other national figures you keep seeing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408126#post1408126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before the tangent were my joke about Gods getting gigs as comic book superheroes was taken way too seriously we were discussing why American symbol and the USA is demonized around here.<br /> <br /> America is not alone as an exception, both Canada and New Zealand did better, but to paint America as an exceptional force of evil is simply wrong and corrupt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dear Sir, I would definitely urge caution about accusing us of trying to demonize anyone just by offering opinions. A less charitable reader might think you'd be willing to 'kick any and all basic human rights to the curb'... and we wouldn't want that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 08-14-2020, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T06:30:04-07:00","id":1408141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408134#post1408134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is one hell of a claim to make less than a week after the anniversary of the Hiroshima and Nagasaki bombings and while there are ongoing human rights violations declared as such by international organizations both in the actions of the US National Guard against the BLM protesters and in the concentration camps set up for immigrants.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I look at the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nanjing_Massacre\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nanjing_Massacre</a> Nanjing Massacre, where more people were tortured to death by hand than died in both Atom Bomb attacks and a Nanjing was not at the time a significant military target, Both Hiroshima and Nagasaki were legitimate military targets, the so-called peace monument was a military command center.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you have any evidence of these claims? Like, I'm not going to paint China, which is currently enacting a genocide (Uyghurs) and violating international treaties just to curb free speech (Hongkong), not to mention their everyday abuses, as an in any way legitimate regime. But I've never heard of this massive genocide you are speaking of, one that would have had to take place some time in the Stone Age (and then, it would be very hard to prove those other ethnicities were systematically killed) to fit into what I learned in the way of Chinese archaeological chronology. Historically, we have ample evidence of how the multi-ethnic, multi-religious make-up that defines China today came about. And there was absolutely colonialism and genocide involved there, particularly along the southern borders, and that should be addressed more. These historical events don't obscure either the horrors China perpetrates today, nor those the US does. </div> </div> </div>I have neither a copy of the relevant issues of Discovery, Scientific American, nor the Academic journals they cited. But I'm certain you can look them up in any Univerisity library.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are Thanksgiving celebrations that erase the violence enacted by the Pilgrims against the very nations that helped them an acknowledgement of the truth (<a href=\"https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2019/11/25/the-invention-of-thanksgiving)?\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2...thanksgiving)?</a> Are school books that teach children that enslaved Africans were no more than &quot;immigrant workers&quot; acknowledging the truth (<a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2015/10/06/us/publisher-promises-revisions-after-textbook-refers-to-african-slaves-as-workers.html)?\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.nytimes.com/2015/10/06/u...workers.html)?</a> I'm sorry, but this is plain historical whitewashing. No one says that other countries don't share the US's dismal historical record (though few can rival its present negative impact, just think of the Iraq War). The problem lies <i>precisely</i> in a continued <i>lack</i> of acknowledgement, and in a continuation of the injustice founded in colonial times. As federal bodies withhold aid from Native tribes, as reservations are kept food deserts and often lack clean water, as reservations and whole tribes are legally dissolved because of business interests, as police violence against Black Americans and the prison industry attached to it continue a legacy of racism, segregation, and enslavement, the truth of history is <i>not</i> acknlowledged, but tacitly continued as a reign of injustice in the present. And <i>that</i> is why the writers of this game have decided to take more time and wordcount for Columbia - she isn't cut, you won't have to live without the fully fictional deification of your national symbol - the only such, at that, in a game that is otherwise about real-world religions. You'll just have to wait while people take the time to address some sensitive issues. And if you see that as unjustified demonisation of your country already, I think you really need to examine the stance you take both to your country and to the entertainment you consume. </div> </div> </div>I was referencing histories. I've seen an 1810s Pennsylvania school textbook that referenced the idea that the Native Americans were there first and lived in settled towns. I've seen modern textbooks, including my own grade school and high school textbooks that had chapters on the Incas, the Aztecs, and the peoples of North America, and I was born in 1960. And my school textbooks told about African American slavery and it's violent cruelty even in grade school textbooks in the 1960s. Do you know anything about how people lived and acted in the past? Do you care?<br /> <br /> The USA had anti-racist organizations from the 1780s on including anti-slavery movements founded by Ben Franklin, and similar groups co-founded by Franklin and Paine (but the only things more buried than racism in American history is White Anti-Racism). Still I suppose none of this interests you. You'll see no good in America and no evil anywhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T06:47:50-07:00","id":1408144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408141#post1408141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I look at the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nanjing_Massacre\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nanjing_Massacre</a> Nanjing Massacre, where more people were tortured to death by hand than died in both Atom Bomb attacks and a Nanjing was not at the time a significant military target, Both Hiroshima and Nagasaki were legitimate military targets, the so-called peace monument was a military command center.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fail to see how what happened in Nanjing in 1937/38 justifies what happened at Hiroshima and Nagasaki in 1945. Two wrongs don't make a right, as is so often say. Civilian populations are <i>never</i> valid targets for weapons of mass destruction. Not to mention that Japan was already offering capitulation at this point and that the internal communications of the US government and military, which were already released in the 1970s, show clearly that this class A war crime was committed for the sole reason of showing off the new technology to the Soviets. They wanted to see how many people those bombs could kill, so they dropped them on the most populous cities they could find; they wanted to see what the bombs would do to survivors, so they sent in doctors afterwards for some frankly grotesque experiments. I have seen photos of the samples they took, that stuff ain't pretty. Nanjing was a horrific war crime that Japan still hasn't properly stood up for as a nation, but there <i>were</i> trials and death sentences for high-ranking members of the Japanese government and military. There were no such consequences for the US. Both Nanjing and Hiroshima/Nagasaki were brutal, cruel, and unnecessary war crimes and neither justifies the other. I will say that the way you try to measure and weigh against each other different kinds of pain and death to justify your own idea of the spotless, &quot;noble&quot; history of your country is sickening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have neither a copy of the relevant issues of Discovery, Scientific American, nor the Academic journals they cited. But I'm certain you can look them up in any Univerisity library. </div> </div> </div>You are certain, are you? How the Hell am I supposed to find them when you won't even give me the issue numbers?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you know anything about how people lived and acted in the past? Do you care? </div> </div> </div>Hi. I'm a historian. This is my job. I care. A lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You'll see no good in America and no evil anywhere else. </div> </div> </div>It's sentences like these that always make me wonder, Astromancer, whether you read my replies to you at all (I mean, in all fairness, you once told me you don't). I literally discussed Chinese human rights and international law violations right there for context. Saying I &quot;see no evil anywhere else&quot; is just an empty, pre-minted phrase that has no relation to what I actually wrote. You went and resurrected the &quot;America is demonised&quot; line of discussion there after the conversation had already moved on. You clearly want to address an issue here. Good. Great. But then <i>please</i> interact with the other people in the room and don't just pile non-sequiturs on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T07:02:39-07:00","id":1408146,"title":"","content":"Here we go again.<br /> <br /> People, calm down please! You guys takes all to personal and lose track of the discussion (in this case, Columbia RAW was a good portrait of the image Americans from the 1800s had of America).<br /> <br /> People are horrible, were horrible and will be horrible for many more generations before we start really respecting each other, so let\u2019s just calm down and discuss the book before this tread is closed/blocked.<br /> <br /> Thank you all!<br /> <br /> Edit: By the way, Columbia is not in the book anymore (except for her picture), so National Gods (to differentiate from cultural gods) is not a official thing for a couple more years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-14-2020, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T07:12:07-07:00","id":1408147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408141#post1408141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was referencing histories. I've seen an 1810s Pennsylvania school textbook that referenced the idea that the Native Americans were there first and lived in settled towns. I've seen modern textbooks, including my own grade school and high school textbooks that had chapters on the Incas, the Aztecs, and the peoples of North America, and I was born in 1960. And my school textbooks told about African American slavery and it's violent cruelty even in grade school textbooks in the 1960s. Do you know anything about how people lived and acted in the past? Do you care?<br /> <br /> The USA had anti-racist organizations from the 1780s on including anti-slavery movements founded by Ben Franklin, and similar groups co-founded by Franklin and Paine (but the only things more buried than racism in American history is White Anti-Racism).</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, how strange. It's almost like American history (like most histories) contains moments of great progress, liberation, and high ideals <i>and</i> horrible historical atrocities that should never be ignored or forgotten. Weird, that. Now just imagine trying to adequately capture all that historical baggage in one 300 word write-up for a fictional god for your fantasy RPG?<br /> <br /> As Geoffrey points out, this thread is not about the history of America or about the merits and problems with including Columbia as a goddess. The writers have realised that a god they wanted to write up requires more work than they expected. That's basically it, isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1d6MGe0uK0nLsOABBu3YymfU-7gS7Nwur/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Th\u1ea7n of Vietnam</a>","edited":{"userid":25842,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25842-mr-wopsle","user":"Mr Wopsle","date":".  Spelling 08-14-2020, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25842-mr-wopsle","name":"Mr Wopsle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25842_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T07:15:52-07:00","id":1408148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408141#post1408141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have neither a copy of the relevant issues of Discovery, Scientific American, nor the Academic journals they cited. But I'm certain you can look them up in any Univerisity library.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you make a claim, it's your job to prove that claim, not your opponent's job. I think we can both agree that this is only reasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408141#post1408141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was referencing histories. I've seen an 1810s Pennsylvania school textbook that referenced the idea that the Native Americans were there first and lived in settled towns. I've seen modern textbooks, including my own grade school and high school textbooks that had chapters on the Incas, the Aztecs, and the peoples of North America, and I was born in 1960. And my school textbooks told about African American slavery and it's violent cruelty even in grade school textbooks in the 1960s. Do you know anything about how people lived and acted in the past? Do you care?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your textbooks should not have to be congratulated for conveying historical truth. Of course they reference the idea that the Native Americans were there first, that's why they're called <i>Native Americans</i>. Your textbooks should not need to be congratulated for talking about the cruelty of slavery because <i>that's their job</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408141#post1408141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The USA had anti-racist organizations from the 1780s on including anti-slavery movements founded by Ben Franklin, and similar groups co-founded by Franklin and Paine (but the only things more buried than racism in American history is White Anti-Racism). Still I suppose none of this interests you. You'll see no good in America and no evil anywhere else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, and the first Jacobin club in India was founded in 1794 under the rule of Tipu Sultan of Mysore, but as you might note there were kingdoms and principalities in India for a whole lot longer than 1794. There were also anti-colonization movements in Great Britain and France but that does not erase the horrors that those colonial empires inflicted upon countless people. That America abolished slavery and went to war over that cause is laudable, but we shouldn't forget that America also maintained that slavery for longer than any other Western state than the <i>fucking </i><i>Russian Empire </i>and that even after abolishing slavery, attempts to reconstruct and to permanently leave it in the pages of history were constantly hampered and frustrated at every turn. You cannot selectively choose to remember the anti-racism clubs while forgetting their systematically enabled opposition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":6042,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","user":"ManusDomine","date":". 08-14-2020, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T08:05:52-07:00","id":1408154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408146#post1408146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here we go again.<br /> <br /> People, calm down please! You guys takes all to personal and lose track of the discussion (in this case, Columbia RAW was a good portrait of the image Americans from the 1800s had of America).<br /> <br /> People are horrible, were horrible and will be horrible for many more generations before we start really respecting each other, so let\u2019s just calm down and discuss the book before this tread is closed/blocked.<br /> <br /> Thank you all!<br /> <br /> Edit: By the way, Columbia is not in the book anymore (except for her picture), so National Gods (to differentiate from cultural gods) is not a official thing for a couple more years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err\u2026 there <i>are</i> a couple of references to Columbia in officially published material (I forget if it's Origins or Hero); so technically National Gods <i>are</i> a thing \u2014 and more specifically, Columbia is a thing. It's just that she doesn't (yet) have an official write-up. Which, as I said in my last post, is fine by me. <br /> <br /> I'll also add that part of what makes this a touchy subject for Scion is that it's a game about myth and legend. Even where the cultural gods are concerned, the focus is on how they're portrayed in their respective mythologies, moreso than on what the real-world basis for those mythologies may or may not have been. When Onyx Path gets around to publishing Columbia, it is my expectation that she'll be rooted in the ideals that she's supposed to represent, both in terms of how they were originally conceived and how they're developed over the centuries. <br /> <br /> I'm also hoping that when she does eventually get published, it will be alongside Britannia and Marianna (her British and French counterparts) as Scions of Athena who took on Nationalist roles when they achieved apotheosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T08:26:30-07:00","id":1408165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408141#post1408141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(but the only things more buried than racism in American history is White Anti-Racism)</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming such a thing was true, one might assume that the historical trend of white supremacism in America would mean that they're the ones burying such details.<br /> <br /> It doesn't exactly do much to assuage points about the depths of American racial issues to project implications that People of Colour in the country pervasively and maliciously conceal or misconstrue the magnanimity of white people.<br /> <br /> That and all of the irrelevant Whataboutism. I should think that an American publication mostly created by American writers feels more responsibility to how it interacts with topics of historical American self-representation than they can do anything about the history of other countries (which also don't do anything to assuage the need of the world's most powerful country by far to manage its self-image or perspective of other countries).<br /> <br /> Assertions about things stretching back into barely knowable pre-history don't really match up against policies that are much closer to or still taking place within the modern day, unless one intended to cultivate a narrative of &quot;such oppressive structures are inherent and inescapable&quot;. That assertion would be wrong, but it would at least be consistent. Without it, the whataboutism amounts to little more than bombardment with details to force endless qualifiers and explanations that end up muddying conversation and distracting from key points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T08:59:27-07:00","id":1408172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408154#post1408154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err\u2026 there <i>are</i> a couple of references to Columbia in officially published material (I forget if it's Origins or Hero); so technically National Gods <i>are</i> a thing \u2014 and more specifically, Columbia is a thing. It's just that she doesn't (yet) have an official write-up. Which, as I said in my last post, is fine by me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair. I forgot that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll also add that part of what makes this a touchy subject for Scion is that it's a game about myth and legend. Even where the cultural gods are concerned, the focus is on how they're portrayed in their respective mythologies, moreso than on what the real-world basis for those mythologies may or may not have been. When Onyx Path gets around to publishing Columbia, it is my expectation that she'll be rooted in the ideals that she's supposed to represent, both in terms of how they were originally conceived and how they're developed over the centuries. </div> </div> </div>The problem here is that Gods don\u2019t change much, and when they do it\u2019s through Mantles, so I think Columbia may be left as she was first seen, a young lady looking for freedom and space for her citizens to grow, that inspired Independence, occupation of the Wyld west and the bang-bang movies. If want to bring a more modern version of her, based on nowadays America, it would require a new mantle of her. Same way as Ares become Mars, but didn\u2019t stop being Ares.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm also hoping that when she does eventually get published, it will be alongside Britannia and Marianna (her British and French counterparts) as Scions of Athena who took on Nationalist roles when they achieved apotheosis. </div> </div> </div>I am quite anxious to see that too. Mother Russia and some national gods from Latin America would be great too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T08:59:44-07:00","id":1408173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408134#post1408134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is one hell of a claim to make less than a week after the anniversary of the Hiroshima and Nagasaki bombings and while there are ongoing human rights violations declared as such by international organisations both in the actions of the US National Guard against the BLM protesters and in the concentration camps set up for immigrants.<br /> <br /> <br /> Do you have any evidence of these claims? Like, I'm not going to paint China, which is currently enacting a genocide (Uyghurs) and violating international treaties just to curb free speech (Hongkong), not to mention their everyday abuses, as an in any way legitimate regime. But I've never heard of this massive genocide you are speaking of, one that would have had to take place some time in the Stone Age (and then, it would be very hard to prove those other ethnicities were systematically killed) to fit into what I learned in the way of Chinese archaeological chronology. Historically, we have ample evidence of how the multi-ethnic, multi-religious make-up that defines China today came about. And there was absolutely colonialism and genocide involved there, particularly along the southern borders, and that should be addressed more. These historical events don't obscure either the horrors China perpetrates today, nor those the US does.<br /> <br /> <br /> Are Thanksgiving celebrations that erase the violence enacted by the Pilgrims against the very nations that helped them an acknowledgement of the truth (<a href=\"https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2019/11/25/the-invention-of-thanksgiving)?\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2...thanksgiving)?</a> Are school books that teach children that enslaved Africans were no more than &amp;quot;immigrant workers&amp;quot; acknowledging the truth (<a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2015/10/06/us/publisher-promises-revisions-after-textbook-refers-to-african-slaves-as-workers.html)?\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.nytimes.com/2015/10/06/u...workers.html)?</a> I'm sorry, but this is plain historical whitewashing. No one says that other countries don't share the US's dismal historical record (though few can rival its present negative impact, just think of the Iraq War). The problem lies <i>precisely</i> in a continued <i>lack</i> of acknowledgement, and in a continuation of the injustice founded in colonial times. As federal bodies withhold aid from Native tribes, as reservations are kept food deserts and often lack clean water, as reservations and whole tribes are legally dissolved because of business interests, as police violence against Black Americans and the prison industry attached to it continue a legacy of racism, segregation, and enslavement, the truth of history is <i>not</i> acknlowledged, but tacitly continued as a reign of injustice in the present. And <i>that</i> is why the writers of this game have decided to take more time and wordcount for Columbia - she isn't cut, you won't have to live without the fully fictional deification of your national symbol - the only such, at that, in a game that is otherwise about real-world religions. You'll just have to wait while people take the time to address some sensitive issues. And if you see that as unjustified demonisation of your country already, I think you really need to examine the stance you take both to your country and to the entertainment you consume.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like history too (though I\u2019m definitely not a historian) and I totally agree with you.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> I also Liked both of your posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T11:25:28-07:00","id":1408192,"title":"","content":"So in a not-at-all-transparent attempt to move away from Columbia<br /> <br /> Even if you don't plan on using the Teros, I recommend taking a look at their PSP, especially their boon Hypertech Upgrade.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I think Gods can change over time. Like, we can point this out how Gods have shifted over time historically. At what point a slightly different God becomes an entirely different God is a question that I myself am not educated to answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 08-14-2020, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T11:47:19-07:00","id":1408200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408192#post1408192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in a not-at-all-transparent attempt to move away from Columbia<br /> <br /> Even if you don't plan on using the Teros, I recommend taking a look at their PSP, especially their boon Hypertech Upgrade.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I think Gods can change over time. Like, we can point this out how Gods have shifted over time historically. At what point a slightly different God becomes an entirely different God is a question that I myself am not educated to answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even without changing Mantles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T11:56:05-07:00","id":1408205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392310-mysteries-of-the-world-the-scion-second-edition-companion-is-out-to-backers?p=1408126#post1408126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before the tangent were my joke about Gods getting gigs as comic book superheroes was taken way too seriously we were discussing why American symbol and the USA is demonized around here.<br /> <br /> We have pantheons in this game presented as pure and noble in virtue that mandated slavery, genocide, human sacrafise by torture, and worse. Compared to many admired pantheons and deities (and living faiths still practiced) the USA at its worst still looks better even noble. Let's remember that, if you look back far enough, every nation exists because it destroyed other peoples.<br /> <br /> Take China for example. Archeology proves that the area that would become China had a diversity of peoples that makes the five hundred nations of North America seem paltry. These peoples are gone. They were wiped out. They left no trace in the Chinese language, and the Han Chinese have no genetic traces of these peoples in their population. I chose China as the extreme example, but there are many similar examples planetwide. Meanwhile, the USA has substantial Native American populations, programs to preserve Native American languages and cultures, and active reform movements to ameliorate continuing abuses. Many nations deny they even had a history before the present population's arrival and ascendency. America always acknowledged the truth. As an American who can point to ancestry from at least three Native American nations, let me point out that there was intermarriage and minglings of populations.<br /> <br /> America is not alone as an exception, both Canada and New Zealand did better, but to paint America as an exceptional force of evil is simply wrong and corrupt.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Dude, don't say that genocides are things that are okay because &quot;other nations do it too.&quot; Because Canada had a sterilization scandal of Native women just a few years ago--and that just means that's evil shit deserving of LOTS of condemnation.<br /> <br /> I'm giving you a warning for this and also asking you to leave the thread for good.<br /> <br /> Because, seriously, terrible idea.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T11:58:12-07:00","id":1408208,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">In fact, sorry, this thread has gone SERIOUSLY off the rails and there's a multitude of violations of respect both to real world atrocities as well as other posters.<br /> <br /> I'm a closing it.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}